[{:db/id 17592186213004 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-090c9908-d9d1-5e59-8b6d-0af06c1b251a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186213439 :question/problem "The equation \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+ax+b={x}^{2}+10x+24\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $a$ and $b$ are constants. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $a,$ and on the right-hand side it is $10.$ So, we have \n\n$$\na=10.\n$$\n\n- The constant term on the left-hand side is $b,$ and on the right-hand side it is $24.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nb=24.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =10+24 \\\\  & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186210531 :answer-field/correct 17592186210536 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-090c9908-d9d1-5e59-8b6d-0af06c1b251a" :question/id #uuid "090c9908-d9d1-5e59-8b6d-0af06c1b251a" :question/math-academy-id "q-288455" :question/problem "The equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+ux+v={x}^{2}-x+1\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $u$ and $v$ are constants. What is the value of $u+v?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $u,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nu=-1.\n$$\n\n- The constant term on the left-hand side is $v,$ and on the right-hand side it is $1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nv=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u+v & =-1+1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-825ec111-8fef-5db1-a9c2-27ab6f1d4b42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-825ec111-8fef-5db1-a9c2-27ab6f1d4b42" :answer-field/id #uuid "825ec111-8fef-5db1-a9c2-27ab6f1d4b42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-924ee794-d6a4-593d-a93d-b2c314a2846d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-190cbee0-7af2-576e-98ad-a582cb732f98" "answer-a181b8a1-35c7-56bc-a5a7-f50443574e45" "answer-924ee794-d6a4-593d-a93d-b2c314a2846d" "answer-7a1157a8-572c-5cf4-86f8-7272bd09d639" "answer-1bdf64b3-5ded-5be3-9039-ad4566118032"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-190cbee0-7af2-576e-98ad-a582cb732f98" :answer/id #uuid "190cbee0-7af2-576e-98ad-a582cb732f98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a181b8a1-35c7-56bc-a5a7-f50443574e45" :answer/id #uuid "a181b8a1-35c7-56bc-a5a7-f50443574e45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-924ee794-d6a4-593d-a93d-b2c314a2846d" :answer/id #uuid "924ee794-d6a4-593d-a93d-b2c314a2846d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a1157a8-572c-5cf4-86f8-7272bd09d639" :answer/id #uuid "7a1157a8-572c-5cf4-86f8-7272bd09d639" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bdf64b3-5ded-5be3-9039-ad4566118032" :answer/id #uuid "1bdf64b3-5ded-5be3-9039-ad4566118032" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-013fe3a7-9b4e-5fe1-9bf4-78ad7af81a4d" :activity/id #uuid "013fe3a7-9b4e-5fe1-9bf4-78ad7af81a4d" :activity/title "Equating Polynomial Coefficients" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048134 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-4e57b915-7c23-5742-9100-719d0b89ea07" "step-f3b2b462-1f6b-56b5-930b-3e10e7711b0c" "step-eb0762a1-82e2-5ea9-ba93-22a0ea8c9976"] :activity/first-step "step-4e57b915-7c23-5742-9100-719d0b89ea07" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-4e57b915-7c23-5742-9100-719d0b89ea07" :step/id #uuid "4e57b915-7c23-5742-9100-719d0b89ea07" :step/content 17592186213439 :step/next "step-f3b2b462-1f6b-56b5-930b-3e10e7711b0c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f3b2b462-1f6b-56b5-930b-3e10e7711b0c" :step/id #uuid "f3b2b462-1f6b-56b5-930b-3e10e7711b0c" :step/content 17592186297188 :step/next "step-eb0762a1-82e2-5ea9-ba93-22a0ea8c9976" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eb0762a1-82e2-5ea9-ba93-22a0ea8c9976" :step/id #uuid "eb0762a1-82e2-5ea9-ba93-22a0ea8c9976" :step/content "question-090c9908-d9d1-5e59-8b6d-0af06c1b251a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119861 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0207e47c-2942-5ced-8414-95264c8bde68"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0207e47c-2942-5ced-8414-95264c8bde68" :question/id #uuid "0207e47c-2942-5ced-8414-95264c8bde68" :question/math-academy-id "q-5658" :question/problem "![](images/2e/2e054a16d93658d53cc9dc16e3fe5544b9a007721d1d9c2f87581799a6257797.png)\n\nWhat is the diameter of a circle that has an area of $36\\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of a circle is $A=\\pi {r}^{2}$, where $r$ is the radius. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 36\\pi  & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 36\\cancel{\\pi } & =\\cancel{\\pi }{r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =36 \\\\ r & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the diameter is\n\n$$\nd=2\\cdot r=2\\cdot 6=12.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3bee644a-73f2-5d35-892b-6222224db91f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3bee644a-73f2-5d35-892b-6222224db91f" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bee644a-73f2-5d35-892b-6222224db91f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-259964da-e8d1-584f-a47d-4187a4bcd044" :answer-field/choices ["answer-259964da-e8d1-584f-a47d-4187a4bcd044" "answer-beda97a9-4ab0-569e-927e-f09c4d2f3d20" "answer-374ff126-9136-52a2-9c24-06afbd88f83f" "answer-33ee2c32-24ac-5d6c-a2c0-def46f715359" "answer-9583798b-f370-5608-be6f-201e498aa9ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-259964da-e8d1-584f-a47d-4187a4bcd044" :answer/id #uuid "259964da-e8d1-584f-a47d-4187a4bcd044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-beda97a9-4ab0-569e-927e-f09c4d2f3d20" :answer/id #uuid "beda97a9-4ab0-569e-927e-f09c4d2f3d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-374ff126-9136-52a2-9c24-06afbd88f83f" :answer/id #uuid "374ff126-9136-52a2-9c24-06afbd88f83f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33ee2c32-24ac-5d6c-a2c0-def46f715359" :answer/id #uuid "33ee2c32-24ac-5d6c-a2c0-def46f715359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9583798b-f370-5608-be6f-201e498aa9ee" :answer/id #uuid "9583798b-f370-5608-be6f-201e498aa9ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119756 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1c7ac009-3403-59c4-adad-c97136633e2b" "question-78884415-9ec2-5003-9971-d3d9da1f23e6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c7ac009-3403-59c4-adad-c97136633e2b" :question/id #uuid "1c7ac009-3403-59c4-adad-c97136633e2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-53582" :question/problem "What is the area of a circular dinner plate given that its radius is $8\\,\\text{cm}?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/72/7223cab003af57279fc16d8044bd9eae6dbfa6bbfe41433b851ebdafd52e91da.png)\n\n \n\nThe area of the dinner plate  is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot {8}^{2} \\\\  & =64\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1edcd967-7d6c-5932-892a-7a8dee229da8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1edcd967-7d6c-5932-892a-7a8dee229da8" :answer-field/id #uuid "1edcd967-7d6c-5932-892a-7a8dee229da8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3b348032-0523-5bc6-be3d-02aaaa0f92d2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35141247-f3e1-5990-ba0f-9bc6d95fa8b5" "answer-7c50db5f-63f5-5063-9925-f6ec4ff127dd" "answer-62dc01c0-ac9f-55a8-97d8-58206daf5ac2" "answer-3b348032-0523-5bc6-be3d-02aaaa0f92d2" "answer-4f7f24b1-0abd-57b7-93d2-f859b641466d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35141247-f3e1-5990-ba0f-9bc6d95fa8b5" :answer/id #uuid "35141247-f3e1-5990-ba0f-9bc6d95fa8b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c50db5f-63f5-5063-9925-f6ec4ff127dd" :answer/id #uuid "7c50db5f-63f5-5063-9925-f6ec4ff127dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62dc01c0-ac9f-55a8-97d8-58206daf5ac2" :answer/id #uuid "62dc01c0-ac9f-55a8-97d8-58206daf5ac2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b348032-0523-5bc6-be3d-02aaaa0f92d2" :answer/id #uuid "3b348032-0523-5bc6-be3d-02aaaa0f92d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f7f24b1-0abd-57b7-93d2-f859b641466d" :answer/id #uuid "4f7f24b1-0abd-57b7-93d2-f859b641466d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-78884415-9ec2-5003-9971-d3d9da1f23e6" :question/id #uuid "78884415-9ec2-5003-9971-d3d9da1f23e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-79024" :question/problem "What is the area of a circle that has a diameter of $4?$" :question/worked-solution "The radius of a circle is half the diameter. So, the radius of our circle is $r=2.$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7f2ed3a4-ca61-5ce1-89d9-355511e39533"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7f2ed3a4-ca61-5ce1-89d9-355511e39533" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f2ed3a4-ca61-5ce1-89d9-355511e39533" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-21bc70ee-3aa4-5a15-a13b-393c06fe66f6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4a8b7aa7-f777-5613-a453-077e27a21b41" "answer-e4675869-60cd-54e6-8ce6-957f6ff1cc02" "answer-2aaf08f9-085c-56ea-a193-97d47d7a7c3b" "answer-21bc70ee-3aa4-5a15-a13b-393c06fe66f6" "answer-2fd0935c-2821-5b9c-b6d0-877b2c1aed13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a8b7aa7-f777-5613-a453-077e27a21b41" :answer/id #uuid "4a8b7aa7-f777-5613-a453-077e27a21b41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4675869-60cd-54e6-8ce6-957f6ff1cc02" :answer/id #uuid "e4675869-60cd-54e6-8ce6-957f6ff1cc02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2aaf08f9-085c-56ea-a193-97d47d7a7c3b" :answer/id #uuid "2aaf08f9-085c-56ea-a193-97d47d7a7c3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21bc70ee-3aa4-5a15-a13b-393c06fe66f6" :answer/id #uuid "21bc70ee-3aa4-5a15-a13b-393c06fe66f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fd0935c-2821-5b9c-b6d0-877b2c1aed13" :answer/id #uuid "2fd0935c-2821-5b9c-b6d0-877b2c1aed13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-245364c3-4153-568e-865a-04318a8cc074" :activity/id #uuid "245364c3-4153-568e-865a-04318a8cc074" :activity/title "Areas of Circles" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049225 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-312df14d-95e2-5711-b6a4-410aa3c383fb" "step-a9e09edb-4acf-52c7-b158-1173f1f2be15" "step-bb3ad15a-27ed-57cd-85b9-84582d33ba21"] :activity/first-step "step-312df14d-95e2-5711-b6a4-410aa3c383fb" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-312df14d-95e2-5711-b6a4-410aa3c383fb" :step/id #uuid "312df14d-95e2-5711-b6a4-410aa3c383fb" :step/content "question-0207e47c-2942-5ced-8414-95264c8bde68" :step/next "step-a9e09edb-4acf-52c7-b158-1173f1f2be15" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a9e09edb-4acf-52c7-b158-1173f1f2be15" :step/id #uuid "a9e09edb-4acf-52c7-b158-1173f1f2be15" :step/content "question-1c7ac009-3403-59c4-adad-c97136633e2b" :step/next "step-bb3ad15a-27ed-57cd-85b9-84582d33ba21" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bb3ad15a-27ed-57cd-85b9-84582d33ba21" :step/id #uuid "bb3ad15a-27ed-57cd-85b9-84582d33ba21" :step/content "question-78884415-9ec2-5003-9971-d3d9da1f23e6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129451 :question/problem "Given that $a$ is an **irrational** number, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $17$ is rational\n\nII. $17a$ is rational\n\nIII. $a\\cdot 17$ is irrational" :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- the product of two rational numbers is *always* rational:\n\n$$\n\\text{rational}\\times \\text{rational}=\\text{rational}\n$$\n\n- the product of a nonzero rational number and an irrational number is *always* irrational:\n\n$$\n\\text{rational}\\times \\text{irrational}=\\text{irrational}\n$$\n\n- the product of two irrational numbers is *sometimes* rational and *sometimes* irrational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The product of a rational number ($17$) and an irrational number ($a$) is irrational.\n\n- Statement III is true. We know from part II that $17a$ is irrational. And since multiplication is commutative, we conclude that $a\\cdot 17$ is irrational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186126206 :answer-field/correct 17592186126207 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129235 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2b569a4a-634a-5c5d-8e62-c4297125cda8" "question-e5ec21fc-d95b-5a6e-8483-328c912290e8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2b569a4a-634a-5c5d-8e62-c4297125cda8" :question/id #uuid "2b569a4a-634a-5c5d-8e62-c4297125cda8" :question/math-academy-id "q-133670" :question/problem "Given that $a$ is an **irrational** number, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\frac{1}{7}$ is irrational\n\nII. $\\frac{1}{7}+a$ is always irrational\n\nIII. $a-\\frac{1}{7}$ is sometimes rational and sometimes irrational" :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- the sum of two rational numbers is *always* rational:\n\n$$\n\\text{rational}+\\text{rational}=\\text{rational}\n$$\n\n- the sum of a rational number and an irrational number is *always* irrational:\n\n$$\n\\text{rational}+\\text{irrational}=\\text{irrational}\n$$\n\n- the sum of two irrational numbers is *sometimes* rational and *sometimes* irrational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\frac{1}{7}$ is rational and $a$ is irrational, their sum is always an irrational number.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\frac{1}{7}$ is rational and $a$ is irrational, their difference is always an irrational number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bbb07e29-0dfc-5f19-8c86-10222960800a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bbb07e29-0dfc-5f19-8c86-10222960800a" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbb07e29-0dfc-5f19-8c86-10222960800a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4bc3bc0f-8609-527a-aef7-251c33edf7a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-592eee93-53ea-5ef8-a416-d9e903eec0f0" "answer-6f10f982-4e9f-520e-8314-481be6073a3c" "answer-4bc3bc0f-8609-527a-aef7-251c33edf7a8" "answer-7a8a4a04-79cb-50a8-82a9-14ab1f07c5bc" "answer-4afb3715-3f88-56d5-b275-bc81df1d0871"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-592eee93-53ea-5ef8-a416-d9e903eec0f0" :answer/id #uuid "592eee93-53ea-5ef8-a416-d9e903eec0f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f10f982-4e9f-520e-8314-481be6073a3c" :answer/id #uuid "6f10f982-4e9f-520e-8314-481be6073a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bc3bc0f-8609-527a-aef7-251c33edf7a8" :answer/id #uuid "4bc3bc0f-8609-527a-aef7-251c33edf7a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a8a4a04-79cb-50a8-82a9-14ab1f07c5bc" :answer/id #uuid "7a8a4a04-79cb-50a8-82a9-14ab1f07c5bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4afb3715-3f88-56d5-b275-bc81df1d0871" :answer/id #uuid "4afb3715-3f88-56d5-b275-bc81df1d0871" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e5ec21fc-d95b-5a6e-8483-328c912290e8" :question/id #uuid "e5ec21fc-d95b-5a6e-8483-328c912290e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-133671" :question/problem "Given that $a$ is an **irrational** number, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-\\frac{1}{{4}^{12}}$ is irrational\n\nII. $a-\\frac{1}{{4}^{12}}$ is always rational\n\nIII. $a+\\frac{1}{{4}^{12}}$ is sometimes rational and sometimes irrational" :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- the sum of two rational numbers is *always* rational:\n\n$$\n\\text{rational}+\\text{rational}=\\text{rational}\n$$\n\n- the sum of a rational number and an irrational number is *always* irrational:\n\n$$\n\\text{rational}+\\text{irrational}=\\text{irrational}\n$$\n\n- the sum of two irrational numbers is *sometimes* rational and *sometimes* irrational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. Since $-\\frac{1}{{4}^{12}}$ is rational and $a$ is irrational, their sum or difference is always an irrational number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b4cee67-86ab-5077-982d-73159c288590"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b4cee67-86ab-5077-982d-73159c288590" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b4cee67-86ab-5077-982d-73159c288590" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ba0a4dea-a87b-5f8a-a8c1-8a1b2cb1d7c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d3fa6e00-f1ae-53d5-ba58-bc05ad657bc4" "answer-8638d565-4f58-5ed6-9bb5-a0a33a0508a9" "answer-0b1658d7-fb9d-5945-a721-88c70ad2282a" "answer-6968ee8d-91bd-5ab9-bb4d-43e24c86d97a" "answer-ba0a4dea-a87b-5f8a-a8c1-8a1b2cb1d7c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3fa6e00-f1ae-53d5-ba58-bc05ad657bc4" :answer/id #uuid "d3fa6e00-f1ae-53d5-ba58-bc05ad657bc4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8638d565-4f58-5ed6-9bb5-a0a33a0508a9" :answer/id #uuid "8638d565-4f58-5ed6-9bb5-a0a33a0508a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b1658d7-fb9d-5945-a721-88c70ad2282a" :answer/id #uuid "0b1658d7-fb9d-5945-a721-88c70ad2282a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6968ee8d-91bd-5ab9-bb4d-43e24c86d97a" :answer/id #uuid "6968ee8d-91bd-5ab9-bb4d-43e24c86d97a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba0a4dea-a87b-5f8a-a8c1-8a1b2cb1d7c2" :answer/id #uuid "ba0a4dea-a87b-5f8a-a8c1-8a1b2cb1d7c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a2a8669c-ee96-56c4-bb5a-a6fd2bdf735e" :activity/id #uuid "a2a8669c-ee96-56c4-bb5a-a6fd2bdf735e" :activity/title "Sums and Products of Rational and Irrational Numbers" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049796 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-2e9d24d0-afef-510e-9520-1823a6868cfd" "step-777d28dd-d1bc-5505-b0d0-f28dac65000a" "step-3d764519-dc05-5945-a5e0-05d704da56e5"] :activity/first-step "step-2e9d24d0-afef-510e-9520-1823a6868cfd" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2e9d24d0-afef-510e-9520-1823a6868cfd" :step/id #uuid "2e9d24d0-afef-510e-9520-1823a6868cfd" :step/content 17592186129451 :step/next "step-777d28dd-d1bc-5505-b0d0-f28dac65000a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-777d28dd-d1bc-5505-b0d0-f28dac65000a" :step/id #uuid "777d28dd-d1bc-5505-b0d0-f28dac65000a" :step/content "question-2b569a4a-634a-5c5d-8e62-c4297125cda8" :step/next "step-3d764519-dc05-5945-a5e0-05d704da56e5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3d764519-dc05-5945-a5e0-05d704da56e5" :step/id #uuid "3d764519-dc05-5945-a5e0-05d704da56e5" :step/content "question-e5ec21fc-d95b-5a6e-8483-328c912290e8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172024 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-442d41d4-64b6-5c13-9965-e1b753377abb" "question-4df596f3-7605-5476-aed1-e33a4f9ad66d" "question-f9219fe2-5911-57bb-89ea-30d2a8256e49"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-442d41d4-64b6-5c13-9965-e1b753377abb" :question/id #uuid "442d41d4-64b6-5c13-9965-e1b753377abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-93093" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[4]{7x+11}+3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{7x+11}+3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{7x+11}+3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{7x+11} & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no root." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-979c25b1-368c-57a9-a520-1e6925bb31db"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-979c25b1-368c-57a9-a520-1e6925bb31db" :answer-field/id #uuid "979c25b1-368c-57a9-a520-1e6925bb31db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9bb6cd66-f41c-5eb6-8461-fb35f552d80d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bde38374-e2a1-5247-9b57-f68cacfb826c" "answer-af8f1e2a-1bc1-5f57-a33a-4631f51b1179" "answer-fcce51e9-96c5-5943-a86f-056185216518" "answer-4b8d030b-747c-50f7-bfed-0d7b9f175406" "answer-9bb6cd66-f41c-5eb6-8461-fb35f552d80d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bde38374-e2a1-5247-9b57-f68cacfb826c" :answer/id #uuid "bde38374-e2a1-5247-9b57-f68cacfb826c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af8f1e2a-1bc1-5f57-a33a-4631f51b1179" :answer/id #uuid "af8f1e2a-1bc1-5f57-a33a-4631f51b1179" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcce51e9-96c5-5943-a86f-056185216518" :answer/id #uuid "fcce51e9-96c5-5943-a86f-056185216518" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b8d030b-747c-50f7-bfed-0d7b9f175406" :answer/id #uuid "4b8d030b-747c-50f7-bfed-0d7b9f175406" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{33}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bb6cd66-f41c-5eb6-8461-fb35f552d80d" :answer/id #uuid "9bb6cd66-f41c-5eb6-8461-fb35f552d80d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function has no root" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172023 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a9239051-66d6-5587-8b77-ad2324021796" "question-01c856f3-ee69-579a-9f89-fe0fbee2a037"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a9239051-66d6-5587-8b77-ad2324021796" :question/id #uuid "a9239051-66d6-5587-8b77-ad2324021796" :question/math-academy-id "q-102534" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[5]{17-2x}+3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[5]{17-2x}+3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[5]{17-2x}+3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{17-2x} & =-3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[5]{17-2x})^{5} & =(-3)^{5} \\\\ 17-2x & =-243 \\\\ -2x & =-260 \\\\ x & =130\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=130.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5cadf92c-a907-55b9-84ec-8b9165a4e849"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5cadf92c-a907-55b9-84ec-8b9165a4e849" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cadf92c-a907-55b9-84ec-8b9165a4e849" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2194eb1e-7b0d-5edd-85b7-6afbfe23a8c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e861c56-8d02-588c-a58f-376835a97092" "answer-7ca7fe85-63d6-53ae-880b-cfc593ad5c0c" "answer-2194eb1e-7b0d-5edd-85b7-6afbfe23a8c4" "answer-a81c0422-436d-580f-9767-5ba8eab6ddf6" "answer-658bb3fa-2757-5a31-8166-483686e4b0b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e861c56-8d02-588c-a58f-376835a97092" :answer/id #uuid "5e861c56-8d02-588c-a58f-376835a97092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-130" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ca7fe85-63d6-53ae-880b-cfc593ad5c0c" :answer/id #uuid "7ca7fe8