re [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4fccfac-f67f-57ae-85f3-23dd62f93a66" :answer/id #uuid "f4fccfac-f67f-57ae-85f3-23dd62f93a66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e61eca8e-14ab-54c4-ad94-08eb1910feb8" :question/id #uuid "e61eca8e-14ab-54c4-ad94-08eb1910feb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-108073" :question/problem "${log}_{8}⁡({8}^{7})=$" :question/worked-solution "The logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n{log}_{b}⁡({b}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=8$ and $x=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{log}_{8}⁡({8}^{7})=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a3be8dc-1d5d-59cc-95b3-03af33b2fb4e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a3be8dc-1d5d-59cc-95b3-03af33b2fb4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a3be8dc-1d5d-59cc-95b3-03af33b2fb4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6bba5b70-c8d5-58be-9d37-6faff7852146" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e4207623-dab0-5d9b-b03e-704090e79618" "answer-6bba5b70-c8d5-58be-9d37-6faff7852146" "answer-86f365f9-48ea-58f6-a215-e979a92b0ff9" "answer-22541458-e554-52ec-8376-f299f409d8cc" "answer-0dd14dfe-60bb-58a0-bd26-51dc968d9c7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4207623-dab0-5d9b-b03e-704090e79618" :answer/id #uuid "e4207623-dab0-5d9b-b03e-704090e79618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bba5b70-c8d5-58be-9d37-6faff7852146" :answer/id #uuid "6bba5b70-c8d5-58be-9d37-6faff7852146" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86f365f9-48ea-58f6-a215-e979a92b0ff9" :answer/id #uuid "86f365f9-48ea-58f6-a215-e979a92b0ff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22541458-e554-52ec-8376-f299f409d8cc" :answer/id #uuid "22541458-e554-52ec-8376-f299f409d8cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0dd14dfe-60bb-58a0-bd26-51dc968d9c7d" :answer/id #uuid "0dd14dfe-60bb-58a0-bd26-51dc968d9c7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c67b84ce-63b0-5172-a4ca-d019c33deb20" :question/id #uuid "c67b84ce-63b0-5172-a4ca-d019c33deb20" :question/math-academy-id "q-108074" :question/problem "${log}_{2}⁡(256)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $256$ as a power of $2$ (the base of the logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n256={2}^{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n{log}_{2}⁡256={log}_{2}⁡({2}^{8})\n$$\n\nThe logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n{log}_{b}⁡({b}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=2$ and $x=8.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{8})=8\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9fd820ef-fff2-5f6c-af98-72bbd3c74b3d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9fd820ef-fff2-5f6c-af98-72bbd3c74b3d" :answer-field/id #uuid "9fd820ef-fff2-5f6c-af98-72bbd3c74b3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e12d5b5f-3854-5910-856f-c7def5deed84" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd67afec-f7f4-501b-8ba1-2d380416c6da" "answer-6b0176f6-2845-5ac4-bf33-9dd4f6a4bb74" "answer-daa350a1-7446-5c5b-b73f-e62813411938" "answer-33abc188-e8ae-5431-af1f-c273a4223033" "answer-e12d5b5f-3854-5910-856f-c7def5deed84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd67afec-f7f4-501b-8ba1-2d380416c6da" :answer/id #uuid "fd67afec-f7f4-501b-8ba1-2d380416c6da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b0176f6-2845-5ac4-bf33-9dd4f6a4bb74" :answer/id #uuid "6b0176f6-2845-5ac4-bf33-9dd4f6a4bb74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "128" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-daa350a1-7446-5c5b-b73f-e62813411938" :answer/id #uuid "daa350a1-7446-5c5b-b73f-e62813411938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "256" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33abc188-e8ae-5431-af1f-c273a4223033" :answer/id #uuid "33abc188-e8ae-5431-af1f-c273a4223033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e12d5b5f-3854-5910-856f-c7def5deed84" :answer/id #uuid "e12d5b5f-3854-5910-856f-c7def5deed84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8fd2dd92-c19f-59ac-abcb-f54b4019b8cc" :question/id #uuid "8fd2dd92-c19f-59ac-abcb-f54b4019b8cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-66588" :question/problem "${log}_{4}⁡64=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $64$ as a power of $4$ (the base of the logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n64={4}^{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n{log}_{4}⁡64={log}_{4}⁡({4}^{3})\n$$\n\nThe logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n{log}_{b}⁡({b}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=4$ and $x=3.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n{log}_{4}⁡({4}^{3})=3\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8abde62-c2af-5bea-89d6-b23136bae5a1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8abde62-c2af-5bea-89d6-b23136bae5a1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8abde62-c2af-5bea-89d6-b23136bae5a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bf2ff1f9-d4c1-52af-87f3-e719c890e1b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf2ff1f9-d4c1-52af-87f3-e719c890e1b5" "answer-3b8d8649-5cc9-56af-a20d-b5ec14df4541" "answer-e584ee49-7e7f-57f3-93cd-a79fd1d2c286" "answer-052a816a-dd80-53d9-8744-1364e26474e0" "answer-12ff10ec-5a7a-55fc-b908-c9ff4e0c695d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf2ff1f9-d4c1-52af-87f3-e719c890e1b5" :answer/id #uuid "bf2ff1f9-d4c1-52af-87f3-e719c890e1b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b8d8649-5cc9-56af-a20d-b5ec14df4541" :answer/id #uuid "3b8d8649-5cc9-56af-a20d-b5ec14df4541" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e584ee49-7e7f-57f3-93cd-a79fd1d2c286" :answer/id #uuid "e584ee49-7e7f-57f3-93cd-a79fd1d2c286" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-052a816a-dd80-53d9-8744-1364e26474e0" :answer/id #uuid "052a816a-dd80-53d9-8744-1364e26474e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12ff10ec-5a7a-55fc-b908-c9ff4e0c695d" :answer/id #uuid "12ff10ec-5a7a-55fc-b908-c9ff4e0c695d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6c887066-3c08-5cb4-b40e-433eb14c4b31" :question/id #uuid "6c887066-3c08-5cb4-b40e-433eb14c4b31" :question/math-academy-id "q-26042" :question/problem "${log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{81})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $\\frac{1}{81}$ as a power of $3$ (the base of the logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{81}=\\frac{1}{{3}^{4}}={3}^{-4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{81})={log}_{3}⁡({3}^{-4})\n$$\n\nThe logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n{log}_{b}⁡({b}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=3$ and $x=-4.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡({3}^{-4})=-4\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2084aa97-e12f-5fe8-a10d-790d4754b710"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2084aa97-e12f-5fe8-a10d-790d4754b710" :answer-field/id #uuid "2084aa97-e12f-5fe8-a10d-790d4754b710" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-814f1f82-22dc-5c8d-891c-3328494b799e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e4b24d2b-5e6b-5a01-8823-5b502061c87a" "answer-81bd13e4-d7a2-5838-845b-af517aaee57d" "answer-814f1f82-22dc-5c8d-891c-3328494b799e" "answer-81e5843d-2f47-5715-a318-45d7445db611" "answer-04b9b4a1-9068-553a-ae2e-30dbf20be4fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4b24d2b-5e6b-5a01-8823-5b502061c87a" :answer/id #uuid "e4b24d2b-5e6b-5a01-8823-5b502061c87a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81bd13e4-d7a2-5838-845b-af517aaee57d" :answer/id #uuid "81bd13e4-d7a2-5838-845b-af517aaee57d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-814f1f82-22dc-5c8d-891c-3328494b799e" :answer/id #uuid "814f1f82-22dc-5c8d-891c-3328494b799e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81e5843d-2f47-5715-a318-45d7445db611" :answer/id #uuid "81e5843d-2f47-5715-a318-45d7445db611" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04b9b4a1-9068-553a-ae2e-30dbf20be4fa" :answer/id #uuid "04b9b4a1-9068-553a-ae2e-30dbf20be4fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-64f9b7ab-1e87-57f9-b089-cc6f9c501397" :question/id #uuid "64f9b7ab-1e87-57f9-b089-cc6f9c501397" :question/math-academy-id "q-2974" :question/problem "${log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{27})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $\\frac{1}{27}$ as a power of $3$ (the base of the logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{27}=\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}={3}^{-3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{27})={log}_{3}⁡({3}^{-3})\n$$\n\nThe logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n{log}_{b}⁡({b}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=3$ and $x=-3.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡({3}^{-3})=-3\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-495b0eea-23f2-5d2e-91e8-fcc19023131f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-495b0eea-23f2-5d2e-91e8-fc