emy-id "q-108076" :question/problem "Calculate ${log}_{72}⁡(72).$" :question/worked-solution "We have the general rule that:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡n=1\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=72.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n{log}_{72}⁡72=1\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cc3754e4-2314-5993-97b9-7e9cfa346294"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cc3754e4-2314-5993-97b9-7e9cfa346294" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc3754e4-2314-5993-97b9-7e9cfa346294" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ef5b7f0f-32e3-515a-bd56-56eb0051bb9f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b9c6d849-d0bb-517e-b070-3a6e3ac252ad" "answer-ef5b7f0f-32e3-515a-bd56-56eb0051bb9f" "answer-6cde5cd2-e2e9-5557-835f-19622e863fd8" "answer-1cf4a4a3-14bc-51ba-a37c-be18c84ace28" "answer-b4d68802-c015-562c-b0cc-e6654c19cc99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9c6d849-d0bb-517e-b070-3a6e3ac252ad" :answer/id #uuid "b9c6d849-d0bb-517e-b070-3a6e3ac252ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef5b7f0f-32e3-515a-bd56-56eb0051bb9f" :answer/id #uuid "ef5b7f0f-32e3-515a-bd56-56eb0051bb9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cde5cd2-e2e9-5557-835f-19622e863fd8" :answer/id #uuid "6cde5cd2-e2e9-5557-835f-19622e863fd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1cf4a4a3-14bc-51ba-a37c-be18c84ace28" :answer/id #uuid "1cf4a4a3-14bc-51ba-a37c-be18c84ace28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4d68802-c015-562c-b0cc-e6654c19cc99" :answer/id #uuid "b4d68802-c015-562c-b0cc-e6654c19cc99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c8c27c46-9870-56fc-a5a5-2b4126a5a87a" :question/id #uuid "c8c27c46-9870-56fc-a5a5-2b4126a5a87a" :question/math-academy-id "q-99678" :question/problem "${log}_{49}⁡1=$" :question/worked-solution "We have the general rule that:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡1=0\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=49.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n{log}_{49}⁡1=0\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-73a3a919-3efa-512c-905e-cc179ba69334"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73a3a919-3efa-512c-905e-cc179ba69334" :answer-field/id #uuid "73a3a919-3efa-512c-905e-cc179ba69334" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a90fbb54-c764-52eb-972c-94e6caab9816" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8ee6f3f8-ce01-5ad0-83c1-e8c0dccc4a15" "answer-b6466326-9205-557e-877c-277bfa7eccde" "answer-a90fbb54-c764-52eb-972c-94e6caab9816" "answer-ec5539b2-3d07-5096-8003-0d9108bd5aea" "answer-1f333dc9-722f-57ed-a0b0-b154025da415"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ee6f3f8-ce01-5ad0-83c1-e8c0dccc4a15" :answer/id #uuid "8ee6f3f8-ce01-5ad0-83c1-e8c0dccc4a15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6466326-9205-557e-877c-277bfa7eccde" :answer/id #uuid "b6466326-9205-557e-877c-277bfa7eccde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a90fbb54-c764-52eb-972c-94e6caab9816" :answer/id #uuid "a90fbb54-c764-52eb-972c-94e6caab9816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec5539b2-3d07-5096-8003-0d9108bd5aea" :answer/id #uuid "ec5539b2-3d07-5096-8003-0d9108bd5aea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f333dc9-722f-57ed-a0b0-b154025da415" :answer/id #uuid "1f333dc9-722f-57ed-a0b0-b154025da415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065355 :tutorial/content "We can evaluate some logarithm expressions by using the fact that the logarithm reverses the action of the exponent.\n\nThe idea is that the log of a power of the base equals the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log_b(b^x) = x\n$$\n\nFor example, in the case of $\\log_2 \\left( 2^{-1/2}\\right),$ we have $b=2$ and $x=-\\dfrac 1 2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log_2\\left(2^{-1/2}\\right) = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065356 :tutorial/content "When the argument of the logarithm isn't written as an exponential, we can often still evaluate the logarithm. All we need to do is rewrite the argument so that it is in the form $b^x,$ where $b$ is the base of the logarithm.\n\nFor instance, to evaluate $\\log_2\\left( 8\\right),$ we rewrite $8$ as a power of $2$ (the base of the logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n8 = 2^{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\log_{2}{8} = \\log_{2}\\left(2^{3}\\right) .\n$$\n\nNow we can proceed as before. The log of a power of the base equals the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log_b(b^x) = x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b = 2$ and $x = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log_{2}\\left(2^{3}\\right) = 3.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065357 :tutorial/content "Recall that two special cases of exponentials are\n\n$$\nn^0 =1 \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad n^1 =n.\n$$\n\nWhat do these look like in logarithm form? We can use the definition of a logarithm to find out:\n\n$a = {n}^{x}$ is equivalent to $\\log_{n}{a} = {x}.$\n\nUsing the above, we have that $n^0 =1$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\log_n 1 = 0.\n$$\n\nAlso, we have that $n^1 =n$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\log_n n = 1.\n$$\n\nThese are two special values for logarithms that are true for any base $n>0, n \\neq 1.$\n\n**Watch out!** We should always assume that the base $n$ of the logarithm does not equal $1.$ Recall that $\\log_n{a} = x$ is equivalent to\n$a = n^x.$ If $n=1$ that transforms to \n\n$$\na = 1^x.\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two possibilities:\n\n- if $a \\neq 1,$ we get that $a \\neq 1^x$ for any real $x,$ and\n\n- if $a = 1,$ we obtain that $1 = 1^x$ for all real $x.$\n\nIn both cases, the notation $\\log_1{a}$ does not make much sense." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064462 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124451 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cf3c18cd-d64f-5eb9-99df-fc0a97727985"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cf3c18cd-d64f-5eb9-99df-fc0a97727985" :question/id #uuid "cf3c18cd-d64f-5eb9-99df-fc0a97727985" :question/math-academy-id "q-65339" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2)+∇f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2)\\cdot ⟨x-\\frac{\\pi }{2},y-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2)=0.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & ={y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\, & ⇒\\, & {f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2)=(2)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 2)=-4, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & ⇒\\, & {f}_{y}(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 2)+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 2)=-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2) & =⟨-4,-\\pi ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2)+∇\\,f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},2)\\cdot ⟨x-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,y-2⟩ \\\\  & =0+⟨-4,-\\pi ⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,y-2⟩ \\\\  & =-4(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\pi (y-2) \\\\  & =4\\pi -4x-\\pi y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-95092209-0ff6-5c1f-932a-fa94ab6826d5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-95092209-0ff6-5c1f-932a-fa94ab6826d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "95092209-0ff6-5c1f-932a-fa94ab6826d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-89f60499-597c-504c-905d-9aa123018b42" :answer-field/choices ["answer-348d3e63-246e-544f-943d-87eec084c7a9" "answer-8eab8e94-7ae8-562e-b6e4-834aa6cc6887" "answer-89f60499-597c-504c-905d-9aa123018b42" "answer-871ed938-ce33-556f-8ef5-892006482a3d" "answer-d43587aa-caee-5e81-afc1-75cb5372bcd4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-348d3e63-246e-544f-943d-87eec084c7a9" :answer/id #uuid "348d3e63-246e-544f-943d-87eec084c7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈-2\\pi +4x-\\pi y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8eab8e94-7ae8-562e-b6e4-834aa6cc6887" :answer/id #uuid "8eab8e94-7ae8-562e-b6e4-834aa6cc6887" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈-\\frac{1}{2}+\\pi -\\pi x+4y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89f60499-597c-504c-905d-9aa123018b42" :answer/id #uuid "89f60499-597c-504c-905d-9aa123018b42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈4\\pi -4x-\\pi y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-871ed938-ce33-556f-8ef5-892006482a3d" :answer/id #uuid "871ed938-ce33-556f-8ef5-892006482a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈4\\pi -x-2\\pi y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d43587aa-caee-5e81-afc1-75cb5372bcd4" :answer/id #uuid "d43587aa-caee-5e81-afc1-75cb5372bcd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-4x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124610 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-72ddfe60-c39c-529d-b7e5-b5ef0ab41db5" "question-2a3146e0-f24e-5488-9d01-55dfe24a4858"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-72ddfe60-c39c-529d-b7e5-b5ef0ab41db5" :question/id #uuid "72ddfe60-c39c-529d-b7e5-b5ef0ab41db5" :question/math-academy-id "q-98343" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(3,0,4)=-5,\\,{f}_{x}(3,0,4)=3,\\,{f}_{y}(3,0,4)=-1,\\,{f}_{z}(3,0,4)=2.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,0,4)$ estimate the value of $f(2.97,-0.02,3.98).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,0,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(3,0,4)+∇f(3,0,4)\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-0,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =f(3,0,4)+⟨{f}_{x}(3,0,4),{f}_{y}(3,0,4),{f}_{z}(3,0,4)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =-5+⟨3,-1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y,z-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(2.97,-0.02,3.98)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=2.97,$ $y=-0.02,$ and $z=3.98$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.97,-0.02,3.98) & ≈-5+⟨3,-1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨2.97-3,-0.02,3.98-4⟩ \\\\  & =-5+⟨3,-1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.03,-0.02,-0.02⟩ \\\\  & =-5-0.09+0.02-0.04 \\\\  & =-5.11\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7b62e85b-4101-530d-8082-303741e5d581"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7b62e85b-4101-530d-8082-303741e5d581" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b62e85b-4101-530d-8082-303741e5d581" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bead9479-8739-5826-ae34-4afcf877117d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d1051c05-0555-59bf-bd9a-560bd3386e91" "answer-e427de28-f06a-5b57-9189-a092c905fde2" "answer-67dfeaeb-1e41-58cc-9a73-4c453d503c85" "answer-bead9479-8739-5826-ae34-4afcf877117d" "answer-db9225d9-c497-562a-b106-0754baa0db31"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1051c05-0555-59bf-bd9a-560bd3386e91" :answer/id #uuid "d1051c05-0555-59bf-bd9a-560bd3386e91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4.85" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e427de28-f06a-5b57-9189-a092c905fde2" :answer/id #uuid "e427de28-f06a-5b57-9189-a092c905fde2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4.89" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67dfeaeb-1e41-58cc-9a73-4c453d503c85" :answer/id #uuid "67dfeaeb-1e41-58cc-9a73-4c453d503c85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4.93" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bead9479-8739-5826-ae34-4afcf877117d" :answer/id #uuid "bead9479-8739-5826-ae34-4afcf877117d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5.11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db9225d9-c497-562a-b106-0754baa0db31" :answer/id #uuid "db9225d9-c497-562a-b106-0754baa0db31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2a3146e0-f24e-5488-9d01-55dfe24a4858" :question/id #uuid "2a3146e0-f24e-5488-9d01-55dfe24a4858" :question/math-academy-id "q-129665" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,-1,-1)=-1,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y,z)=2x,\\,{f}_{y}(x,y,z)=-2z,\\,{f}_{z}(x,y,z)=-2y.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1,-1),$ estimate the value of $f(1.01,-1.02,-1.03).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,-1,-1)+∇f(1,-1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-(-1),z-(-1)⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1+⟨{f}_{x}(1,-1,-1),{f}_{y}(1,-1,-1),{f}_{z}(1,-1,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(1,-1,-1),$ ${f}_{y}(1,-1,-1)$ and ${f}_{z}(1,-1,-1),$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,-1,-1) & =2(1)=2 \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,-1,-1) & =-2(-1)=2 \\\\ {f}_{z}(1,-1,-1) & =-2(-1)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈-1+⟨2,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z+1⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(1.01,-1.02,-1.03)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.01,y=-1.02$ and $z=-1.03,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.01,-1.02,-1.03) & ≈-1+⟨2,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨1.01-1,-1.02+1,-1.03+1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1+⟨2,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,-0.02,-0.03⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1+2(0.01)+2(-0.02)+2(-0.03) \\\\  & ≈-1+0.02-0.04-0.06 \\\\  & ≈-1.08\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d7da7969-1bfc-5a7a-973b-13d349fbd405"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d7da7969-1bfc-5a7a-973b-13d349fbd405" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7da7969-1bfc-5a7a-973b-13d349fbd405" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-410f0bc0-fa46-543e-a594-c94e9437eab2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8c9c2861-2dbc-526f-80ca-6ca1f0e8b13f" "answer-31371fc5-3db5-5f52-a902-57193843002d" "answer-e9ad5b50-59ef-5132-a6fb-4eb47c9fd526" "answer-410f0bc0-fa46-543e-a594-c94e9437eab2" "answer-29960ef5-732d-5bda-992a-c2410df10260"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c9c2861-2dbc-526f-80ca-6ca1f0e8b13f" :answer/id #uuid "8c9c2861-2dbc-526f-80ca-6ca1f0e8b13f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.88" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31371fc5-3db5-5f52-a902-57193843002d" :answer/id #uuid "31371fc5-3db5-5f52-a902-57193843002d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9ad5b50-59ef-5132-a6fb-4eb47c9fd526" :answer/id #uuid "e9ad5b50-59ef-5132-a6fb-4eb47c9fd526" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.02" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-410f0bc0-fa46-543e-a594-c94e9437eab2" :answer/id #uuid "410f0bc0-fa46-543e-a594-c94e9437eab2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.08" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29960ef5-732d-5bda-992a