$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(4{x}^{6})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(4{x}^{6})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}+1}}\\cdot 24{x}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7980ba46-cdbd-57c7-a587-1058e543ca1f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7980ba46-cdbd-57c7-a587-1058e543ca1f" :answer-field/id #uuid "7980ba46-cdbd-57c7-a587-1058e543ca1f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bf9422de-70d7-5b56-86c9-b6e0e3f8ac48" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf9422de-70d7-5b56-86c9-b6e0e3f8ac48"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf9422de-70d7-5b56-86c9-b6e0e3f8ac48" :answer/id #uuid "bf9422de-70d7-5b56-86c9-b6e0e3f8ac48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{16x^{12}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167333 :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2x,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}+1}}\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186165207 :answer-field/correct "answer-34ca7eb5-470d-5de1-a985-de106f49a368" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a329f99-1cb4-5ae5-986d-04046d4da53b" "answer-5151a771-88dc-542b-a9ae-7d62e4b4c00a" "answer-83532860-31ea-58e2-b9f9-6d535dda8bb1" "answer-2eaac038-f9e7-574a-9d3b-55268419a77d" "answer-34ca7eb5-470d-5de1-a985-de106f49a368"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a329f99-1cb4-5ae5-986d-04046d4da53b" :answer/id #uuid "2a329f99-1cb4-5ae5-986d-04046d4da53b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5151a771-88dc-542b-a9ae-7d62e4b4c00a" :answer/id #uuid "5151a771-88dc-542b-a9ae-7d62e4b4c00a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83532860-31ea-58e2-b9f9-6d535dda8bb1" :answer/id #uuid "83532860-31ea-58e2-b9f9-6d535dda8bb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2eaac038-f9e7-574a-9d3b-55268419a77d" :answer/id #uuid "2eaac038-f9e7-574a-9d3b-55268419a77d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34ca7eb5-470d-5de1-a985-de106f49a368" :answer/id #uuid "34ca7eb5-470d-5de1-a985-de106f49a368" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-81194d8a-eb61-596d-a974-e9c1b95b27d0" :question/id #uuid "81194d8a-eb61-596d-a974-e9c1b95b27d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-342186" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4{x}^{6},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $40{x}^{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(4{x}^{6})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot {(4{x}^{6})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}-1}}\\cdot 24{x}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{40{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6235e9dc-58a1-59ae-99c9-7e3dc3328c5e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6235e9dc-58a1-59ae-99c9-7e3dc3328c5e" :answer-field/id #uuid "6235e9dc-58a1-59ae-99c9-7e3dc3328c5e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-44a5b82a-32ba-5916-9e64-71bad821a989" :answer-field/choices ["answer-44a5b82a-32ba-5916-9e64-71bad821a989"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44a5b82a-32ba-5916-9e64-71bad821a989" :answer/id #uuid "44a5b82a-32ba-5916-9e64-71bad821a989" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{16x^{12}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5cb35406-f881-5edb-97ef-a6166561d9a4" :question/id #uuid "5cb35406-f881-5edb-97ef-a6166561d9a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-337912" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=5\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(5\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-55157626-6033-5874-9ef3-053348b5fbb5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-55157626-6033-5874-9ef3-053348b5fbb5" :answer-field/id #uuid "55157626-6033-5874-9ef3-053348b5fbb5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-de2b3cf5-7996-5a83-8016-0d37e8dd76db" :answer-field/choices ["answer-de2b3cf5-7996-5a83-8016-0d37e8dd76db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de2b3cf5-7996-5a83-8016-0d37e8dd76db" :answer/id #uuid "de2b3cf5-7996-5a83-8016-0d37e8dd76db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{4x^{2}-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-96d64ea4-0cd9-5375-8219-9bae598e5ccf" :question/id #uuid "96d64ea4-0cd9-5375-8219-9bae598e5ccf" :question/math-academy-id "q-96442" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(3x-1)}^{2}}\\cdot {(3x-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(9{x}^{2}-6x+1)}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6x-9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3x(2-3x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-234ebf93-a04c-5d8d-8e1c-b425df18a6da"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-234ebf93-a04c-5d8d-8e1c-b425df18a6da" :answer-field/id #uuid "234ebf93-a04c-5d8d-8e1c-b425df18a6da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-34c509d9-c9e3-5e5a-96bf-5cdd105d47dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-34c509d9-c9e3-5e5a-96bf-5cdd105d47dc" "answer-cdd1ece5-ab7e-5496-92a9-91b0efce86bc" "answer-d5415a38-3db7-5d44-8a65-954ad5158627" "answer-38d279e8-7cae-5b93-951c-3a28c5addc73" "answer-2eac5166-dabb-580e-b725-9123713934f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34c509d9-c9e3-5e5a-96bf-5cdd105d47dc" :answer/id #uuid "34c509d9-c9e3-5e5a-96bf-5cdd105d47dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3x(2-3x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdd1ece5-ab7e-5496-92a9-91b0efce86bc" :answer/id #uuid "cdd1ece5-ab7e-5496-92a9-91b0efce86bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3x(2x-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5415a38-3db7-5d44-8a65-954ad5158627" :answer/id #uuid "d5415a38-3db7-5d44-8a65-954ad5158627" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x(3x-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38d279e8-7cae-5b93-951c-3a28c5addc73" :answer/id #uuid "38d279e8-7cae-5b93-951c-3a28c5addc73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2x(2-3x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2eac5166-dabb-580e-b725-9123713934f7" :answer/id #uuid "2eac5166-dabb-580e-b725-9123713934f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x(3-2x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-70dcb121-2c51-5a9a-a8d4-5a609e0f6393" :question/id #uuid "70dcb121-2c51-5a9a-a8d4-5a609e0f6393" :question/math-academy-id "q-95515" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-6{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{1-6{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-212e29fd-c89d-59da-8733-ca9e159bf6c5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-212e29fd-c89d-59da-8733-ca9e159bf6c5" :answer-field/id #uuid "212e29fd-c89d-59da-8733-ca9e159bf6c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-92cf951f-ffe1-52cb-8388-109ef99e7472" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4dfa4edf-fd9d-5a8f-a626-7170364756b1" "answer-92cf951f-ffe1-52cb-8388-109ef99e7472" "answer-97d1c47e-bdee-5dd8-9638-5da53d198c96" "answer-89ad944e-2be0-56d8-9333-f1471c3d89eb" "answer-aa289fc3-789c-5683-9e2f-a94eb4e15b61"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dfa4edf-fd9d-5a8f-a626-7170364756b1" :answer/id #uuid "4dfa4edf-fd9d-5a8f-a626-7170364756b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{1-4{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92cf951f-ffe1-52cb-8388-109ef99e7472" :answer/id #uuid "92cf951f-ffe1-52cb-8388-109ef99e7472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{1-6{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97d1c47e-bdee-5dd8-9638-5da53d198c96" :answer/id #uuid "97d1c47e-bdee-5dd8-9638-5da53d198c96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{6{x}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89ad944e-2be0-56d8-9333-f1471c3d89eb" :answer/id #uuid "89ad944e-2be0-56d8-9333-f1471c3d89eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{6{x}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa289fc3-789c-5683-9e2f-a94eb4e15b61" :answer/id #uuid "aa289fc3-789c-5683-9e2f-a94eb4e15b61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6{x}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-75d28ef3-1631-5b9b-9daa-067de055774b" :question/id #uuid "75d28ef3-1631-5b9b-9daa-067de055774b" :question/math-academy-id "q-342834" :question/problem "$$\n\nCalculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}  $-\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the quotient rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(\\frac{u}{v})}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, chain rule, and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{2})}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{2})}^{′}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{4}}\\cdot 2x-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{(1-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c6519ced-6442-570a-bd64-3c6fcf3d8465"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c6519ced-6442-570a-bd64-3c6fcf3d8465" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6519ced-6442-570a-bd64-3c6fcf3d8465" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8b0c2e13-f46b-5cc2-a1f8-4fae6a1f6c14" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8b0c2e13-f46b-5cc2-a1f8-4fae6a1f6c14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b0c2e13-f46b-5cc2-a1f8-4fae6a1f6c14" :answer/id #uuid "8b0c2e13-f46b-5cc2-a1f8-4fae6a1f6c14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{(1-x^{4})\\ln x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ea0760db-381e-5949-ad3f-4c6362ce39c8" :question/id #uuid "ea0760db-381e-5949-ad3f-4c6362ce39c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-342829" :question/problem "$$\n\nCalculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=7\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}\\,+$ | $7{e}^{x}\\sqrt{x}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the product rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(u\\cdot v)}{\\text{d}x}={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, chain rule, and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={(7\\sqrt{x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+7\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\text{arsinh}\\,({e}^{x})+7\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {({e}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+7\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+1}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+\\frac{7{e}^{x}\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2359561c-3d9c-533b-8276-68f929336a72"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2359561c-3d9c-533b-8276-68f929336a72" :answer-field/id #uuid "2359561c-3d9c-533b-8276-68f929336a72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d5132a52-9a35-59bb-b61d-b459caa0c29d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d5132a52-9a35-59bb-b61d-b459caa0c29d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5132a52-9a35-59bb-b61d-b459caa0c29d" :answer/id #uuid "d5132a52-9a35-59bb-b61d-b459caa0c29d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{e^{2x}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186068026 :answer-field/choices 17592186068027] [:db/retract 17592186068026 :answer-field/choices 17592186068028] [:db/retract 17592186068026 :answer-field/choices 17592186068029] [:db/retract 17592186068026 :answer-field/choices 17592186068031] [:db/retract 17592186067792 :answer-field/choices 17592186067793] [:db/retract 17592186067792 :answer-field/choices 17592186067794] [:db/retract 17592186067792 :answer-field/choices 17592186067795] [:db/retract 17592186067792 :answer-field/choices 17592186067796] [:db/retract 17592186067792 :answer-field/choices 17592186067797] {:db/id 17592186068705 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-54e8fcf4-d538-5483-805d-02e6f387fbe1" "question-6745c884-99da-504f-8dea-4d79761c7ad9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068559 :question/problem "What are the solutions to $x^2 + 16 = 0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tx^2 + 16 &= 0 \\[3pt]\n\t\tx^2 &= -16\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = \\pm \\sqrt{-16}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-16} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x = \\pm 4 \\textrm{i}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068706 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cd11ce23-27fe-5c7c-9502-a02ca58513ca" "question-77b8b796-0079-55bf-a33c-a1e9a651dc45"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068560 :question/problem "If $p^2 + 27 = 0,$ then $p =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\np^2 + 27 & = 0\\[3pt]\n\np^2 & = -27 \n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\np = \\pm \\sqrt{-27}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $p$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\\pm \\sqrt{-27} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{27\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{27}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{{3}^{2}\\cdot 3}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $p = \\pm 3\\sqrt{3} \\, \\textrm{i}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068707 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-400405cc-0be2-5aff-a15c-d39026e0c0e5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068561 :question/problem "If $16z^2 + 49 = 0,$ then $z =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n16z^2 + 49 & = 0\\[5pt]\n\n16z^2 & = -49 \\[5pt]\n\nz^2 & = -\\dfrac{49}{16}\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nz = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\dfrac{49}{16}}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $z$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{49}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{16}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{16}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{49}}{\\sqrt{16}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{7}{4}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=\\pm \\dfrac{7}{4} \\textrm{i}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068708 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4f3f1aa3-5d05-5a94-a6c1-299187fd64c9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068562 :question/problem "What are the solutions of the equation $2y^2 + 9 = 0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t2y^2 + 9 &= 0 \\[5pt]\n\n\t\t2y^2 &= -9\\[5pt]\n\ny^2 & = -\\dfrac{9}{2}\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain\n\n$$\ny = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\dfrac{9}{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{9}{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=\\pm \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\textrm{i}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-54e8fcf4-d538-5483-805d-02e6f387fbe1" :question/id #uuid "54e8fcf4-d538-5483-805d-02e6f387fbe1" :question/math-academy-id "q-3798" :question/problem "Determine the solutions of the equation ${f}^{2}=-25.$" :question/worked-solution "By taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nf=\\pm \\sqrt{-25}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $f$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f & =\\pm \\sqrt{-25} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{25\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-034b99ab-70ba-5ad6-bd7c-9dda87ca0e9a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-034b99ab-70ba-5ad6-bd7c-9dda87ca0e9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "034b99ab-70ba-5ad6-bd7c-9dda87ca0e9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-266bfaba-e0ad-54ed-a64f-4f4ffbfb8902" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ac9eda6d-045e-5a51-b62d-88f1c1e340cc" "answer-e1ec939f-0273-5f44-8255-e8b1ba57b46b" "answer-d8e8a1fd-a135-5c2b-9ac9-41a7a4d9916c" "answer-4b1ab51e-19e4-5940-bf86-98f1edbcd396" "answer-266bfaba-e0ad-54ed-a64f-4f4ffbfb8902"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac9eda6d-045e-5a51-b62d-88f1c1e340cc" :answer/id #uuid "ac9eda6d-045e-5a51-b62d-88f1c1e340cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1ec939f-0273-5f44-8255-e8b1ba57b46b" :answer/id #uuid "e1ec939f-0273-5f44-8255-e8b1ba57b46b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8e8a1fd-a135-5c2b-9ac9-41a7a4d9916c" :answer/id #uuid "d8e8a1fd-a135-5c2b-9ac9-41a7a4d9916c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b1ab51e-19e4-5940-bf86-98f1edbcd396" :answer/id #uuid "4b1ab51e-19e4-5940-bf86-98f1edbcd396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-266bfaba-e0ad-54ed-a64f-4f4ffbfb8902" :answer/id #uuid "266bfaba-e0ad-54ed-a64f-4f4ffbfb8902" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 5\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6745c884-99da-504f-8dea-4d79761c7ad9" :question/id #uuid "6745c884-99da-504f-8dea-4d79761c7ad9" :question/math-academy-id "q-3800" :question/problem "Find the solutions of $-2{d}^{2}-32=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{d}^{2}-32 & =0 \\\\ -2{d}^{2} & =32 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nd=\\pm \\sqrt{-16}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $d$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\pm \\sqrt{-16} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3be83e8b-5545-56ff-8f99-b342e2d41b6d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3be83e8b-5545-56ff-8f99-b342e2d41b6d" :answer-field/id #uuid "3be83e8b-5545-56ff-8f99-b342e2d41b6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6e10b4a5-c145-5f33-bc00-5b55f1b12b7e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-42a6b18e-fce9-5676-9bb3-b8c41c919f98" "answer-0d188e9b-c8ce-5dcf-9c36-a3861cf5517e" "answer-b3bbdea5-c901-5b65-a473-79724ef31de3" "answer-6e10b4a5-c145-5f33-bc00-5b55f1b12b7e" "answer-f7ba722e-1c0b-582b-9f92-61a5ecf03ed5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42a6b18e-fce9-5676-9bb3-b8c41c919f98" :answer/id #uuid "42a6b18e-fce9-5676-9bb3-b8c41c919f98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d188e9b-c8ce-5dcf-9c36-a3861cf5517e" :answer/id #uuid "0d188e9b-c8ce-5dcf-9c36-a3861cf5517e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3bbdea5-c901-5b65-a473-79724ef31de3" :answer/id #uuid "b3bbdea5-c901-5b65-a473-79724ef31de3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e10b4a5-c145-5f33-bc00-5b55f1b12b7e" :answer/id #uuid "6e10b4a5-c145-5f33-bc00-5b55f1b12b7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7ba722e-1c0b-582b-9f92-61a5ecf03ed5" :answer/id #uuid "f7ba722e-1c0b-582b-9f92-61a5ecf03ed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 8\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cd11ce23-27fe-5c7c-9502-a02ca58513ca" :question/id #uuid "cd11ce23-27fe-5c7c-9502-a02ca58513ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-66250" :question/problem "If ${y}^{2}+63=0,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+63 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\sqrt{-63}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-63} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{63\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{63}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-01c4d03b-0f6c-5ed2-bb6c-7ece815cef7a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-01c4d03b-0f6c-5ed2-bb6c-7ece815cef7a" :answer-field/id #uuid "01c4d03b-0f6c-5ed2-bb6c-7ece815cef7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-968e606e-ef3a-548c-83db-9562168f22c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d622d75e-b7ed-55dc-a703-128ef32c46fc" "answer-04435194-583c-5f60-9dfd-01b9700b130f" "answer-5c3f02bd-55b2-5559-aeb7-4f037f158d53" "answer-968e606e-ef3a-548c-83db-9562168f22c3" "answer-0c227682-8093-5ef5-81a9-3967ae571e70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d622d75e-b7ed-55dc-a703-128ef32c46fc" :answer/id #uuid "d622d75e-b7ed-55dc-a703-128ef32c46fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04435194-583c-5f60-9dfd-01b9700b130f" :answer/id #uuid "04435194-583c-5f60-9dfd-01b9700b130f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c3f02bd-55b2-5559-aeb7-4f037f158d53" :answer/id #uuid "5c3f02bd-55b2-5559-aeb7-4f037f158d53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-968e606e-ef3a-548c-83db-9562168f22c3" :answer/id #uuid "968e606e-ef3a-548c-83db-9562168f22c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 3\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c227682-8093-5ef5-81a9-3967ae571e70" :answer/id #uuid "0c227682-8093-5ef5-81a9-3967ae571e70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 7\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-77b8b796-0079-55bf-a33c-a1e9a651dc45" :question/id #uuid "77b8b796-0079-55bf-a33c-a1e9a651dc45" :question/math-academy-id "q-112361" :question/problem "If $\\frac{{w}^{2}}{4}+22=0,$ then $w=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{w}^{2}}{4}+22 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{{w}^{2}}{4} & =-22 \\\\ {w}^{2} & =-88\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nw=\\pm \\sqrt{-88}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $w$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =\\pm \\sqrt{-88} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{88\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{88}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d2ce979-7e0d-5596-bf06-3e1a04e2c43e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d2ce979-7e0d-5596-bf06-3e1a04e2c43e" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d2ce979-7e0d-5596-bf06-3e1a04e2c43e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6d2fa09f-bb3c-500a-95e5-cd60c937e500" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ed1bc14-82fb-5586-8801-a9b3e6b4e62f" "answer-5cff7245-7201-59d9-87b6-8026bdec1e7d" "answer-6d2fa09f-bb3c-500a-95e5-cd60c937e500" "answer-ef11576a-065b-5597-a05f-5c52d3c4c3c3" "answer-082df12d-a520-52a4-a79f-c0349cc96c96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ed1bc14-82fb-5586-8801-a9b3e6b4e62f" :answer/id #uuid "4ed1bc14-82fb-5586-8801-a9b3e6b4e62f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cff7245-7201-59d9-87b6-8026bdec1e7d" :answer/id #uuid "5cff7245-7201-59d9-87b6-8026bdec1e7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d2fa09f-bb3c-500a-95e5-cd60c937e500" :answer/id #uuid "6d2fa09f-bb3c-500a-95e5-cd60c937e500" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef11576a-065b-5597-a05f-5c52d3c4c3c3" :answer/id #uuid "ef11576a-065b-5597-a05f-5c52d3c4c3c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-082df12d-a520-52a4-a79f-c0349cc96c96" :answer/id #uuid "082df12d-a520-52a4-a79f-c0349cc96c96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-400405cc-0be2-5aff-a15c-d39026e0c0e5" :question/id #uuid "400405cc-0be2-5aff-a15c-d39026e0c0e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-112392" :question/problem "Solve the equation $64{x}^{2}+25=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64{x}^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ 64{x}^{2} & =-25 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-\\frac{25}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{25}{64}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{25}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{64}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8ba00ab0-0740-5e8c-a650-8814201a3289"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8ba00ab0-0740-5e8c-a650-8814201a3289" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ba00ab0-0740-5e8c-a650-8814201a3289" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-969f1e9e-4b76-5c2c-bf53-cb282cd406bc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0556a39-a30a-5103-8ac8-b9fd9c124181" "answer-f4a37dfe-add9-5f03-af56-5005240e24ba" "answer-969f1e9e-4b76-5c2c-bf53-cb282cd406bc" "answer-bcfad2dd-2a87-5e60-8f2d-670b7ad0671e" "answer-cf368447-cb6f-5846-b336-75bdcf7ac676"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0556a39-a30a-5103-8ac8-b9fd9c124181" :answer/id #uuid "f0556a39-a30a-5103-8ac8-b9fd9c124181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4a37dfe-add9-5f03-af56-5005240e24ba" :answer/id #uuid "f4a37dfe-add9-5f03-af56-5005240e24ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-969f1e9e-4b76-5c2c-bf53-cb282cd406bc" :answer/id #uuid "969f1e9e-4b76-5c2c-bf53-cb282cd406bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcfad2dd-2a87-5e60-8f2d-670b7ad0671e" :answer/id #uuid "bcfad2dd-2a87-5e60-8f2d-670b7ad0671e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{8}{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf368447-cb6f-5846-b336-75bdcf7ac676" :answer/id #uuid "cf368447-cb6f-5846-b336-75bdcf7ac676" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{8}}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069476 :question/problem "Find the solutions of the equation $25{z}^{2}+36=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{z}^{2}+36 & =0 \\\\ 25{z}^{2} & =-36 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =-\\frac{36}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nz=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{36}{25}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $z$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{36}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{36}{25}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{36}{25}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{36}}{\\sqrt{25}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068026 :answer-field/correct "answer-6cc99135-04a4-5f4d-9082-3578e0f40e55" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba415c2b-05c1-5eab-bbbc-b63c56c7ee81" "answer-eaaee2d2-b7a1-54d7-9520-3d7345cdf5c0" "answer-19fd0de6-fe5b-5d65-b618-614985030ff0" "answer-6cc99135-04a4-5f4d-9082-3578e0f40e55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba415c2b-05c1-5eab-bbbc-b63c56c7ee81" :answer/id #uuid "ba415c2b-05c1-5eab-bbbc-b63c56c7ee81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eaaee2d2-b7a1-54d7-9520-3d7345cdf5c0" :answer/id #uuid "eaaee2d2-b7a1-54d7-9520-3d7345cdf5c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{5}{6}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19fd0de6-fe5b-5d65-b618-614985030ff0" :answer/id #uuid "19fd0de6-fe5b-5d65-b618-614985030ff0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{6}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cc99135-04a4-5f4d-9082-3578e0f40e55" :answer/id #uuid "6cc99135-04a4-5f4d-9082-3578e0f40e55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069437 :question/problem "What are the solutions of the equation $8{y}^{2}+12=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{y}^{2}+12 & =0 \\\\ 8{y}^{2} & =-12 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{12}{8} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186067792 :answer-field/correct "answer-132d8079-9184-5cf8-ba4f-984356f42abc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8cb3719-cc2d-5ddd-9d2c-3c62af520a87" "answer-75ddc0a8-68a7-598b-8764-ca68b1936025" "answer-5c0134ef-4a13-5729-92c1-c572b616051a" "answer-132d8079-9184-5cf8-ba4f-984356f42abc" "answer-38dd3953-965d-5e7d-8ae6-4d3ca4fb8eed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8cb3719-cc2d-5ddd-9d2c-3c62af520a87" :answer/id #uuid "b8cb3719-cc2d-5ddd-9d2c-3c62af520a87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75ddc0a8-68a7-598b-8764-ca68b1936025" :answer/id #uuid "75ddc0a8-68a7-598b-8764-ca68b1936025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c0134ef-4a13-5729-92c1-c572b616051a" :answer/id #uuid "5c0134ef-4a13-5729-92c1-c572b616051a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-132d8079-9184-5cf8-ba4f-984356f42abc" :answer/id #uuid "132d8079-9184-5cf8-ba4f-984356f42abc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38dd3953-965d-5e7d-8ae6-4d3ca4fb8eed" :answer/id #uuid "38dd3953-965d-5e7d-8ae6-4d3ca4fb8eed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4f3f1aa3-5d05-5a94-a6c1-299187fd64c9" :question/id #uuid "4f3f1aa3-5d05-5a94-a6c1-299187fd64c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-113227" :question/problem "What are the solutions of the equation $27{y}^{2}+63=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27{y}^{2}+63 & =0 \\\\ 27{y}^{2} & =-63 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{63}{27} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{7}{3}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{7}{3}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e455b236-f5ba-5efb-9cf8-947f74de5bc5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e455b236-f5ba-5efb-9cf8-947f74de5bc5" :answer-field/id #uuid "e455b236-f5ba-5efb-9cf8-947f74de5bc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b56fdb14-e345-575d-98f5-ff9d20c0bf6f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b56fdb14-e345-575d-98f5-ff9d20c0bf6f" "answer-e8c03e9a-9191-5060-bf9e-79f75effd569" "answer-93f2873d-9ebc-5f6a-8df6-69bfb7ebcbba" "answer-a4da0f14-5e09-529a-95ca-9379f4a7f02f" "answer-0c8d2c96-bf75-5f7c-985e-6f68a2e4ae27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b56fdb14-e345-575d-98f5-ff9d20c0bf6f" :answer/id #uuid "b56fdb14-e345-575d-98f5-ff9d20c0bf6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8c03e9a-9191-5060-bf9e-79f75effd569" :answer/id #uuid "e8c03e9a-9191-5060-bf9e-79f75effd569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{9}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93f2873d-9ebc-5f6a-8df6-69bfb7ebcbba" :answer/id #uuid "93f2873d-9ebc-5f6a-8df6-69bfb7ebcbba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4da0f14-5e09-529a-95ca-9379f4a7f02f" :answer/id #uuid "a4da0f14-5e09-529a-95ca-9379f4a7f02f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c8d2c96-bf75-5f7c-985e-6f68a2e4ae27" :answer/id #uuid "0c8d2c96-bf75-5f7c-985e-6f68a2e4ae27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{9}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069964 :tutorial/content "When solving an equation, we sometimes require taking the square root of a negative number. In such cases, we will not end up with real solutions, but imaginary solutions.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's solve the equation $2x^2 +8 = 0$ for $x.$ First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t2x^2 + 8 &= 0 \\[3pt]\n\t\t2x^2 &= -8 \\[3pt]\n\t\tx^2 &= -4\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = \\pm \\sqrt{-4}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-4} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{4\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x = \\pm 2 \\textrm{i}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068991 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198415 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5810c34a-c4d1-5c91-ad48-b47e68d3d961"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5810c34a-c4d1-5c91-ad48-b47e68d3d961" :question/id #uuid "5810c34a-c4d1-5c91-ad48-b47e68d3d961" :question/math-academy-id "q-163495" :question/problem "![](images/85/8524ffd2ff653703bd6fcfa2b44d36821aeb34877d58bbc6df388497cac8e07d.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $x$-axis and the lines $y=2x$ and $y=4-2x$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{y}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/29/293f8454cdda5897de111d6444baa4674eccf28a36e2053f3f2cb71f948e07fe.png)\n\n  \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{2-y/2}\\frac{x}{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{2-y/2}x(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4)[{\\int }_{y/2}^{2-y/2}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4){[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=y/2}^{x=2-y/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[{(2-\\frac{y}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{y}{2})}^{2}]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4)(4-2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}-2{y}^{3}+12{y}^{2}-24y+16\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}+4{y}^{3}-12{y}^{2}+16y]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(-8+32-48+32) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5bd3a5dd-dd4c-547c-b5d1-8d0a45894fb2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5bd3a5dd-dd4c-547c-b5d1-8d0a45894fb2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5bd3a5dd-dd4c-547c-b5d1-8d0a45894fb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ca5ecce-5260-5c1e-8f33-b8f542d178e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3072f94c-01b5-54a9-b170-a51dc79492ef" "answer-0ca5ecce-5260-5c1e-8f33-b8f542d178e6" "answer-5eaedd3e-5549-5a47-bec3-16e990341664" "answer-d55eae46-1605-5397-8e51-d16aa7ce1714" "answer-b151edaa-d755-5566-a03a-6ad23995bfa1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3072f94c-01b5-54a9-b170-a51dc79492ef" :answer/id #uuid "3072f94c-01b5-54a9-b170-a51dc79492ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ca5ecce-5260-5c1e-8f33-b8f542d178e6" :answer/id #uuid "0ca5ecce-5260-5c1e-8f33-b8f542d178e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5eaedd3e-5549-5a47-bec3-16e990341664" :answer/id #uuid "5eaedd3e-5549-5a47-bec3-16e990341664" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d55eae46-1605-5397-8e51-d16aa7ce1714" :answer/id #uuid "d55eae46-1605-5397-8e51-d16aa7ce1714" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b151edaa-d755-5566-a03a-6ad23995bfa1" :answer/id #uuid "b151edaa-d755-5566-a03a-6ad23995bfa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281671 :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=y-x.$ Find the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=-2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198416 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f58ffe9b-0496-58b1-afb0-490bd07410f5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284385 :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f58ffe9b-0496-58b1-afb0-490bd07410f5" :question/id #uuid "f58ffe9b-0496-58b1-afb0-490bd07410f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-163644" :question/problem "![](images/16/1664a86a1fee25cccbb710ad4335e4d69b36c24d64c95ae7bff9e54d2ac3a6b6.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $x=\\sqrt{2y}$ and $x=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{4}{3},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2y}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/d9/d9c529fe2d238a3d6ac4e20cfcd571f980c28a4eb2c13497fab3ccb0d15ac6eb.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{3M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}\\frac{3M}{4}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-2)^{2}[x]_{x={y}^{2}/2}^{x=\\sqrt{2y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-2)^{2}(\\sqrt{2y}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\sqrt{2}{y}^{5/2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}-4\\sqrt{2}{y}^{3/2}+2{y}^{3}+4\\sqrt{2}{y}^{1/2}-2{y}^{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{[\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}{y}^{7/2}}{7}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{10}-\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}{y}^{5/2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}+\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}{y}^{3/2}}{3}-\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}(\\frac{32}{7}-\\frac{32}{10}-\\frac{64}{5}+8+\\frac{32}{3}-\\frac{16}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}(\\frac{40}{21}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10M}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35069258-2167-5032-8d01-4365ee34fd5e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35069258-2167-5032-8d01-4365ee34fd5e" :answer-field/id #uuid "35069258-2167-5032-8d01-4365ee34fd5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c8bb2c02-211c-5a2e-a640-026cbe50166a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2eacb6ae-6056-590f-819d-a963272134e3" "answer-35a9c1f4-2e16-576e-924a-d4b678c80437" "answer-c8bb2c02-211c-5a2e-a640-026cbe50166a" "answer-772eaf55-132c-5352-905f-c57fafed7229" "answer-91698260-fd1f-560e-af4f-3325f33e5dab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2eacb6ae-6056-590f-819d-a963272134e3" :answer/id #uuid "2eacb6ae-6056-590f-819d-a963272134e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35a9c1f4-2e16-576e-924a-d4b678c80437" :answer/id #uuid "35a9c1f4-2e16-576e-924a-d4b678c80437" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8bb2c02-211c-5a2e-a640-026cbe50166a" :answer/id #uuid "c8bb2c02-211c-5a2e-a640-026cbe50166a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10M}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-772eaf55-132c-5352-905f-c57fafed7229" :answer/id #uuid "772eaf55-132c-5352-905f-c57fafed7229" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12M}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91698260-fd1f-560e-af4f-3325f33e5dab" :answer/id #uuid "91698260-fd1f-560e-af4f-3325f33e5dab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8M}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198418 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c9bc333f-6b0c-5f6d-9c9d-d8671bcc2662"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c9bc333f-6b0c-5f6d-9c9d-d8671bcc2662" :question/id #uuid "c9bc333f-6b0c-5f6d-9c9d-d8671bcc2662" :question/math-academy-id "q-163668" :question/problem "![](images/de/de1ac9ccf84134913bbf8847ea9795a1ec83084602db705c8bef723897e7bd92.png)\n\nA triangular plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed between the axes and the line $y=1-x.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/a0/a092d57585bd7b2803473c30328dd72f82a6611d8398de821099db72e2ed3621.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-3|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k|x|=kx,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}kx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[y]}_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}x(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=kx=6Mx.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}6Mx\\,|x-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}6Mx(x-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+9x)[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+9x){[y]}_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+9x)(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-{x}^{4}+7{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+9x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{7}{4}{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =6M[-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{7}{4}-5+\\frac{9}{2}-0] \\\\  & =6M[\\frac{21}{20}] \\\\  & =\\frac{63M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3ba9cf1e-7b09-5bd1-9530-9886c7103582"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3ba9cf1e-7b09-5bd1-9530-9886c7103582" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ba9cf1e-7b09-5bd1-9530-9886c7103582" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-97a1c003-97ab-53e3-ace4-a7b2493ed8a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6af1bedd-39d1-53f8-a5fa-012aad761837" "answer-2e86dacb-298b-544e-9c38-9ba72f2fd531" "answer-ed99f3ae-797d-5ac0-9a9e-b9fcda70eaa0" "answer-9a2bbd50-7d0e-58aa-a9e9-5914bb7ed4fa" "answer-97a1c003-97ab-53e3-ace4-a7b2493ed8a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6af1bedd-39d1-53f8-a5fa-012aad761837" :answer/id #uuid "6af1bedd-39d1-53f8-a5fa-012aad761837" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19M}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e86dacb-298b-544e-9c38-9ba72f2fd531" :answer/id #uuid "2e86dacb-298b-544e-9c38-9ba72f2fd531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21M}{40}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed99f3ae-797d-5ac0-9a9e-b9fcda70eaa0" :answer/id #uuid "ed99f3ae-797d-5ac0-9a9e-b9fcda70eaa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23M}{120}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a2bbd50-7d0e-58aa-a9e9-5914bb7ed4fa" :answer/id #uuid "9a2bbd50-7d0e-58aa-a9e9-5914bb7ed4fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23M}{40}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97a1c003-97ab-53e3-ace4-a7b2493ed8a4" :answer/id #uuid "97a1c003-97ab-53e3-ace4-a7b2493ed8a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{63M}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-fc7eec98-73ca-5474-8f13-04b32db6392e" :activity/id #uuid "fc7eec98-73ca-5474-8f13-04b32db6392e" :activity/title "Moments of Inertia of Laminas About Other Axes" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048585 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-b4eb2f43-d2cd-51a1-99f9-5fba6e8ad21f" "step-91404c15-d1ad-50fd-86be-ced9527f549e" "step-43368631-ebb7-5e59-8710-99f4db8da10e" "step-ca887437-9db2-5a07-9af6-a9d5c2c7ebbe" "step-49428a33-5d98-5966-ad50-cdf5ae5c8855"] :activity/first-step "step-b4eb2f43-d2cd-51a1-99f9-5fba6e8ad21f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-b4eb2f43-d2cd-51a1-99f9-5fba6e8ad21f" :step/id #uuid "b4eb2f43-d2cd-51a1-99f9-5fba6e8ad21f" :step/content "question-5810c34a-c4d1-5c91-ad48-b47e68d3d961" :step/next "step-91404c15-d1ad-50fd-86be-ced9527f549e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-91404c15-d1ad-50fd-86be-ced9527f549e" :step/id #uuid "91404c15-d1ad-50fd-86be-ced9527f549e" :step/content 17592186281671 :step/next "step-43368631-ebb7-5e59-8710-99f4db8da10e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-43368631-ebb7-5e59-8710-99f4db8da10e" :step/id #uuid "43368631-ebb7-5e59-8710-99f4db8da10e" :step/content 17592186284385 :step/next "step-ca887437-9db2-5a07-9af6-a9d5c2c7ebbe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ca887437-9db2-5a07-9af6-a9d5c2c7ebbe" :step/id #uuid "ca887437-9db2-5a07-9af6-a9d5c2c7ebbe" :step/content "question-f58ffe9b-0496-58b1-afb0-490bd07410f5" :step/next "step-49428a33-5d98-5966-ad50-cdf5ae5c8855" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-49428a33-5d98-5966-ad50-cdf5ae5c8855" :step/id #uuid "49428a33-5d98-5966-ad50-cdf5ae5c8855" :step/content "question-c9bc333f-6b0c-5f6d-9c9d-d8671bcc2662" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231427 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6127495a-5135-5ebc-930f-1823afa46170" "question-5fd4a0bf-2844-5191-8ab1-3fd5afa7e748"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6127495a-5135-5ebc-930f-1823afa46170" :question/id #uuid "6127495a-5135-5ebc-930f-1823afa46170" :question/math-academy-id "q-94240" :question/problem "The position $y(t),$ measured in meters, of a particle oscillating with periodically forced harmonic motion without damping is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡pt+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. Which value of the parameter $p$ causes the oscillator to resonate?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of forced harmonic motion without damping is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t).\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ here represents simple harmonic motion, and it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants of integration.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=3\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{3}t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{3}t.\n$$\n\nThe oscillator experiences resonance when the frequency $p$ of the external periodic force $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡pt+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡pt$ coincides with the frequency of the complementary solution, which is $\\omega =\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the oscillator experiences resonance when $p=\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fb900ce9-eab3-5acd-b944-c83320b552a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fb900ce9-eab3-5acd-b944-c83320b552a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb900ce9-eab3-5acd-b944-c83320b552a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5cf5111e-dd21-52f0-ba55-7a49bf7ac9de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3a645be0-c56e-5fba-b4a4-a98456908295" "answer-b985565e-b931-58c3-9ed9-2657a34e2b19" "answer-47adda2a-334d-5928-b439-90caf6b3f1a2" "answer-8227aecf-efb6-5968-88a7-e86a8151635a" "answer-5cf5111e-dd21-52f0-ba55-7a49bf7ac9de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a645be0-c56e-5fba-b4a4-a98456908295" :answer/id #uuid "3a645be0-c56e-5fba-b4a4-a98456908295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b985565e-b931-58c3-9ed9-2657a34e2b19" :answer/id #uuid "b985565e-b931-58c3-9ed9-2657a34e2b19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47adda2a-334d-5928-b439-90caf6b3f1a2" :answer/id #uuid "47adda2a-334d-5928-b439-90caf6b3f1a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8227aecf-efb6-5968-88a7-e86a8151635a" :answer/id #uuid "8227aecf-efb6-5968-88a7-e86a8151635a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cf5111e-dd21-52f0-ba55-7a49bf7ac9de" :answer/id #uuid "5cf5111e-dd21-52f0-ba55-7a49bf7ac9de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5fd4a0bf-2844-5191-8ab1-3fd5afa7e748" :question/id #uuid "5fd4a0bf-2844-5191-8ab1-3fd5afa7e748" :question/math-academy-id "q-343666" :question/problem "The position $y(t),$ measured in meters, of a particle oscillating with periodically forced harmonic motion without damping is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+18y=6{sin}^{2}⁡pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. Which value of the parameter $p$ causes the oscillator to resonate?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of forced harmonic motion without damping is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t).\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ here represents simple harmonic motion, and it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants of integration.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=18\\,⟹\\,\\omega =3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\sqrt{2}t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\sqrt{2}t).\n$$\n\nThe oscillator experiences resonance when the frequency of the external periodic force $f(t)=6{sin}^{2}⁡pt$ is equal to the frequency of the complementary solution, which is $\\omega =3\\sqrt{2}.$ Since \n\n$$\nf(t)=6{sin}^{2}⁡pt=3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2pt,\n$$\n\nthe frequency of the external periodic force is $2p.$\n\nTherefore, the oscillator experiences resonance when $p=\\frac{\\omega }{2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eff11dfc-8ed3-50df-b798-7c071f983a45"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eff11dfc-8ed3-50df-b798-7c071f983a45" :answer-field/id #uuid "eff11dfc-8ed3-50df-b798-7c071f983a45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d6d57042-0b74-581c-8b12-7c36887caccc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-20deeaf4-0740-55aa-9dcb-2e6f140632ee" "answer-d6d57042-0b74-581c-8b12-7c36887caccc" "answer-1dd368cc-9a2b-551e-b564-ee313f513e46" "answer-79c50765-9d84-524e-b588-8c069de3e84d" "answer-fb517908-0db1-516e-8b98-2030ddb3dcdb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20deeaf4-0740-55aa-9dcb-2e6f140632ee" :answer/id #uuid "20deeaf4-0740-55aa-9dcb-2e6f140632ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6d57042-0b74-581c-8b12-7c36887caccc" :answer/id #uuid "d6d57042-0b74-581c-8b12-7c36887caccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dd368cc-9a2b-551e-b564-ee313f513e46" :answer/id #uuid "1dd368cc-9a2b-551e-b564-ee313f513e46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79c50765-9d84-524e-b588-8c069de3e84d" :answer/id #uuid "79c50765-9d84-524e-b588-8c069de3e84d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb517908-0db1-516e-8b98-2030ddb3dcdb" :answer/id #uuid "fb517908-0db1-516e-8b98-2030ddb3dcdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-4d9716c2-538f-569a-b8a0-0013d0209d04" :activity/id #uuid "4d9716c2-538f-569a-b8a0-0013d0209d04" :activity/title "Resonance in Vibrating Systems" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048966 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-6ea7ee19-1db2-5615-9f9e-e31df6e39383" "step-373883cf-0b34-53c8-a1b3-d0897fad83b2" "step-88f88f3d-b294-5d78-b139-7b4adde6210f" "step-f52a8e3f-5139-540f-bde0-174c3dc62d36" "step-d88d67e5-0c3f-5914-b3bd-6949d7868fd1"] :activity/first-step "step-6ea7ee19-1db2-5615-9f9e-e31df6e39383" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-6ea7ee19-1db2-5615-9f9e-e31df6e39383" :step/id #uuid "6ea7ee19-1db2-5615-9f9e-e31df6e39383" :step/content "question-6127495a-5135-5ebc-930f-1823afa46170" :step/next "step-373883cf-0b34-53c8-a1b3-d0897fad83b2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-373883cf-0b34-53c8-a1b3-d0897fad83b2" :step/id #uuid "373883cf-0b34-53c8-a1b3-d0897fad83b2" :step/content "question-5fd4a0bf-2844-5191-8ab1-3fd5afa7e748" :step/next "step-88f88f3d-b294-5d78-b139-7b4adde6210f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-88f88f3d-b294-5d78-b139-7b4adde6210f" :step/id #uuid "88f88f3d-b294-5d78-b139-7b4adde6210f" :step/content 17592186495094 :step/next "step-f52a8e3f-5139-540f-bde0-174c3dc62d36" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f52a8e3f-5139-540f-bde0-174c3dc62d36" :step/id #uuid "f52a8e3f-5139-540f-bde0-174c3dc62d36" :step/content 17592186317423 :step/next "step-d88d67e5-0c3f-5914-b3bd-6949d7868fd1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d88d67e5-0c3f-5914-b3bd-6949d7868fd1" :step/id #uuid "d88d67e5-0c3f-5914-b3bd-6949d7868fd1" :step/content 17592186317433 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064363 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2b95da98-1f5f-5fa5-ad72-3959a1d46504"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2b95da98-1f5f-5fa5-ad72-3959a1d46504" :question/id #uuid "2b95da98-1f5f-5fa5-ad72-3959a1d46504" :question/math-academy-id "q-2129" :question/problem "$5\\cdot (-5)=$" :question/worked-solution "We have a product of a positive number $(5)$ and a negative number $(-5).$ So the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n5\\cdot (-5)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $5$ by $5$ without any signs: $5\\cdot 5=25.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n5\\cdot (-5)=-25.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b5d7548f-4651-5714-a212-98fe6364d378"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b5d7548f-4651-5714-a212-98fe6364d378" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5d7548f-4651-5714-a212-98fe6364d378" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-133dff8c-5de2-5a42-af45-1dc2089abeef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2396cb0f-cf6c-5511-a0cf-32332fccd198" "answer-133dff8c-5de2-5a42-af45-1dc2089abeef" "answer-0411dfeb-e3a8-5dc4-9b78-e2d3d9b02b15" "answer-994b30f4-895d-550b-ab51-e6d5983c68e7" "answer-aeb70b96-6db0-5bcc-b838-a7e4522e3491"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2396cb0f-cf6c-5511-a0cf-32332fccd198" :answer/id #uuid "2396cb0f-cf6c-5511-a0cf-32332fccd198" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-133dff8c-5de2-5a42-af45-1dc2089abeef" :answer/id #uuid "133dff8c-5de2-5a42-af45-1dc2089abeef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0411dfeb-e3a8-5dc4-9b78-e2d3d9b02b15" :answer/id #uuid "0411dfeb-e3a8-5dc4-9b78-e2d3d9b02b15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-994b30f4-895d-550b-ab51-e6d5983c68e7" :answer/id #uuid "994b30f4-895d-550b-ab51-e6d5983c68e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aeb70b96-6db0-5bcc-b838-a7e4522e3491" :answer/id #uuid "aeb70b96-6db0-5bcc-b838-a7e4522e3491" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064256 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-38fc7adf-0452-58e7-9840-3560c89df130"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-38fc7adf-0452-58e7-9840-3560c89df130" :question/id #uuid "38fc7adf-0452-58e7-9840-3560c89df130" :question/math-academy-id "q-236832" :question/problem "$6-43=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $43$ is larger than $6,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n43-6\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,3\\end{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,13\\end{aligned} \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  &  & \\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n43-6=37.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n6-43=-37.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53ee380b-dbad-5bda-b397-5e40d67dcaef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53ee380b-dbad-5bda-b397-5e40d67dcaef" :answer-field/id #uuid "53ee380b-dbad-5bda-b397-5e40d67dcaef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c71f521f-acfa-538e-b4a4-b5ccf0744921" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c71f521f-acfa-538e-b4a4-b5ccf0744921"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c71f521f-acfa-538e-b4a4-b5ccf0744921" :answer/id #uuid "c71f521f-acfa-538e-b4a4-b5ccf0744921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-37" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171933 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bd6001aa-5beb-57ae-855c-a9db7b063e64"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bd6001aa-5beb-57ae-855c-a9db7b063e64" :question/id #uuid "bd6001aa-5beb-57ae-855c-a9db7b063e64" :question/math-academy-id "q-85435" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $26\\,489\\,225$\n\nII. $14\\,736\\,438$\n\nIII. $749\\,356\\,314$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $26\\,489\\,225$ is not divisible by $2,$ so it is not divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- The number $14\\,736\\,438$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+4+7+3+6+4+3+8=36\n$$\n\nSo, $14\\,736\\,438$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $749\\,356\\,314$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n7+4+9+3+5+6+3+1+4=42\n$$\n\nSo, $749\\,356\\,314$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bdc5610c-12bb-5623-b3c8-987e1a880e7f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bdc5610c-12bb-5623-b3c8-987e1a880e7f" :answer-field/id #uuid "bdc5610c-12bb-5623-b3c8-987e1a880e7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e3a8e7a6-c558-5c83-9825-bcf1b0f38adf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-67027953-9b36-5a07-91c8-e63f2d9c44d0" "answer-9735e0c8-6095-51ae-8f1f-6a22cd6c37b2" "answer-e3a8e7a6-c558-5c83-9825-bcf1b0f38adf" "answer-ff608879-f846-5e5f-a92a-af8609b27731" "answer-0aa071bc-3705-5e8f-a8c4-66af19f5f97a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67027953-9b36-5a07-91c8-e63f2d9c44d0" :answer/id #uuid "67027953-9b36-5a07-91c8-e63f2d9c44d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9735e0c8-6095-51ae-8f1f-6a22cd6c37b2" :answer/id #uuid "9735e0c8-6095-51ae-8f1f-6a22cd6c37b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3a8e7a6-c558-5c83-9825-bcf1b0f38adf" :answer/id #uuid "e3a8e7a6-c558-5c83-9825-bcf1b0f38adf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff608879-f846-5e5f-a92a-af8609b27731" :answer/id #uuid "ff608879-f846-5e5f-a92a-af8609b27731" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0aa071bc-3705-5e8f-a8c4-66af19f5f97a" :answer/id #uuid "0aa071bc-3705-5e8f-a8c4-66af19f5f97a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147544 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-38eccaa1-2de4-5013-b379-9718f328c233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-38eccaa1-2de4-5013-b379-9718f328c233" :question/id #uuid "38eccaa1-2de4-5013-b379-9718f328c233" :question/math-academy-id "q-350272" :question/problem "Ella and Nora run bakeries. In the previous week, $10%$ of Ella’s pastries were gluten-free, while the decimal proportion of Nora’s pastries that were gluten-free was $0.05.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than one fourth of Ella's pastries were gluten-free.\n\nII. More than one fourth of Nora's pastries were gluten-free.\n\nIII. Ella had a greater percentage of gluten-free pastries compared to Nora." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n10%<\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 100%=25%,\n$$\n\nless than one-fourth of Ella's pastries were gluten-free.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n0.05<\\frac{1}{4}=0.25.\n$$\n\nSo, less than one-fourth of Nora's pastries were gluten-free.\n\n- Statement III is true. We can compare $10%$ and $0.05$ by converting the decimal into a percent.\n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.05\\times 100=5%\n$$\n\nSince $10%>5%,$ Ella had a **greater** percentage of gluten-free pastries compared to Nora.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-252ef2a1-dcf1-50c9-9860-56f9e9785136"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-252ef2a1-dcf1-50c9-9860-56f9e9785136" :answer-field/id #uuid "252ef2a1-dcf1-50c9-9860-56f9e9785136" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ba920345-040b-5c00-9222-48c01b435190" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba920345-040b-5c00-9222-48c01b435190" "answer-ea490ea3-55ec-50ba-b568-f292077c0820" "answer-3d95e62e-9e4b-5826-9690-2dd1c535569f" "answer-d67c4190-47a5-58db-9d33-fefd4a5da6e6" "answer-47461420-eebc-5210-9f02-135bf2199ac7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba920345-040b-5c00-9222-48c01b435190" :answer/id #uuid "ba920345-040b-5c00-9222-48c01b435190" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea490ea3-55ec-50ba-b568-f292077c0820" :answer/id #uuid "ea490ea3-55ec-50ba-b568-f292077c0820" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d95e62e-9e4b-5826-9690-2dd1c535569f" :answer/id #uuid "3d95e62e-9e4b-5826-9690-2dd1c535569f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d67c4190-47a5-58db-9d33-fefd4a5da6e6" :answer/id #uuid "d67c4190-47a5-58db-9d33-fefd4a5da6e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47461420-eebc-5210-9f02-135bf2199ac7" :answer/id #uuid "47461420-eebc-5210-9f02-135bf2199ac7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073786 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7fc0e3a0-04f8-58fa-8d72-05025f5c40e7" "question-8c4f25cf-0173-54ec-98c6-ab10b632fa9a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7fc0e3a0-04f8-58fa-8d72-05025f5c40e7" :question/id #uuid "7fc0e3a0-04f8-58fa-8d72-05025f5c40e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-60254" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a37bbb00bcf37dce19970f5494412eaa9c68e5db134354e3c9d790cd9dc7a5b5.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of triangles to squares?" :question/worked-solution "We count the number of triangles. We see that there is $1$ triangle.\n\n We count the number of square. We see that there are $3$ squares.\n\nSo the ratio of triangles to squares is $\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c968ce86-4d0c-5e9e-8768-5180c33c524e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c968ce86-4d0c-5e9e-8768-5180c33c524e" :answer-field/id #uuid "c968ce86-4d0c-5e9e-8768-5180c33c524e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a47150a2-4d2c-528f-86a0-ceb4e70b28ff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8e9a1a6-a981-5a12-836d-7987e291ca25" "answer-a47150a2-4d2c-528f-86a0-ceb4e70b28ff" "answer-4aa36735-7bbe-5b13-ab8f-722801427503" "answer-de19f2d7-b048-5fd2-a5d0-b10b55dad122" "answer-2de39e75-06fe-5828-9b1e-26772a43909d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8e9a1a6-a981-5a12-836d-7987e291ca25" :answer/id #uuid "d8e9a1a6-a981-5a12-836d-7987e291ca25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a47150a2-4d2c-528f-86a0-ceb4e70b28ff" :answer/id #uuid "a47150a2-4d2c-528f-86a0-ceb4e70b28ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4aa36735-7bbe-5b13-ab8f-722801427503" :answer/id #uuid "4aa36735-7bbe-5b13-ab8f-722801427503" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de19f2d7-b048-5fd2-a5d0-b10b55dad122" :answer/id #uuid "de19f2d7-b048-5fd2-a5d0-b10b55dad122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2de39e75-06fe-5828-9b1e-26772a43909d" :answer/id #uuid "2de39e75-06fe-5828-9b1e-26772a43909d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054808 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c49fa7b3-27b5-573b-aadb-233575243dcc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c49fa7b3-27b5-573b-aadb-233575243dcc" :question/id #uuid "c49fa7b3-27b5-573b-aadb-233575243dcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-109030" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the point $D(-5,4)?$" :question/worked-solution "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $D.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $D$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-5,$ so we move $5$ units to the *left*, in the negative direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $D$ has a $y$-coordinate of $4,$ so we move $4$ units *up*, in the positive direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/19/19520b88504572a892e70dc3a40d16a3635c8528f9e591ac82aa0411d8091129.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-63b03bab-6a94-55d1-98c6-554a345ccc3e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-63b03bab-6a94-55d1-98c6-554a345ccc3e" :answer-field/id #uuid "63b03bab-6a94-55d1-98c6-554a345ccc3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7d868048-21b4-5600-937d-9be2d5b10f59" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7d868048-21b4-5600-937d-9be2d5b10f59" "answer-6b558799-faf9-534e-aa65-41d66e79512e" "answer-247b63ff-ef4c-59a6-8a1c-d39e