n-3851cb9c-32ab-50a5-b26d-1f3dac949677" :step/next "step-66e17220-fc20-5871-9abf-d593d06ab365" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-66e17220-fc20-5871-9abf-d593d06ab365" :step/id #uuid "66e17220-fc20-5871-9abf-d593d06ab365" :step/content "question-a98d2b92-1f79-5299-a15c-071e314b9a2c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162092 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4429ddaa-a525-58c0-92b3-0e53fe11c811"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162356 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -60 \\\\ -60 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}80 & -60 \\\\ -60 & 45\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=80+45+6=131.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159338 :answer-field/correct 17592186159343 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-4429ddaa-a525-58c0-92b3-0e53fe11c811" :question/id #uuid "4429ddaa-a525-58c0-92b3-0e53fe11c811" :question/math-academy-id "q-158687" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 7 \\\\ 7 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {3}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}14 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 17\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=14+17+(-11)=20.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-202094ff-d5d0-573f-8726-95ed023974e0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-202094ff-d5d0-573f-8726-95ed023974e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "202094ff-d5d0-573f-8726-95ed023974e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f1d38658-fd1d-5ce3-b87a-8e86e685face" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1d38658-fd1d-5ce3-b87a-8e86e685face" "answer-dd6971fb-f55c-5b45-a29a-c0b1c6b3fce9" "answer-79e70a70-5d0e-5891-8648-6f2603f7c863" "answer-345c0919-c48a-51ec-93ba-67d74c6a767d" "answer-c3cdfeea-ed07-56b9-8520-05327e82865e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1d38658-fd1d-5ce3-b87a-8e86e685face" :answer/id #uuid "f1d38658-fd1d-5ce3-b87a-8e86e685face" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd6971fb-f55c-5b45-a29a-c0b1c6b3fce9" :answer/id #uuid "dd6971fb-f55c-5b45-a29a-c0b1c6b3fce9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31