step-dbe4af0f-6deb-5714-9b84-7310ef2b54a2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dbe4af0f-6deb-5714-9b84-7310ef2b54a2" :step/id #uuid "dbe4af0f-6deb-5714-9b84-7310ef2b54a2" :step/content "question-4429ddaa-a525-58c0-92b3-0e53fe11c811" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073879 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0b38d5e8-3d9c-538c-a4ad-3e7a464487ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0b38d5e8-3d9c-538c-a4ad-3e7a464487ac" :question/id #uuid "0b38d5e8-3d9c-538c-a4ad-3e7a464487ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-60241" :question/problem "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nTo make a delicious soup, Alice requires $3$ grams of ginger powder and $4$ grams of garlic powder, among other ingredients, so she needs $\\boxed{}$ grams of ginger powder for each gram of garlic." :question/worked-solution "The ratio of the number of grams of ginger powder to the number of grams of garlic powder is  $3:4.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nThis means that there is $\\frac{3}{4}$ grams of ginger powder for each gram of garlic powder." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-59a82adf-56d5-585e-b666-ca74577ba041"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-59a82adf-56d5-585e-b666-ca74577ba041" :answer-field/id #uuid "59a82adf-56d5-585e-b666-ca74577ba041" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7fd3c60d-64f1-59ef-990a-4ae04dc3e8c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-47510a96-f323-5933-b408-18ebc0d385e2" "answer-7fd3c60d-64f1-59ef-990a-4ae04dc3e8c7" "answer-7f39009f-6a2e-5d88-a632-2c103dc99418" "answer-6e680698-5ff8-54db-b218-a63ea07e3ee5" "answer-53d98170-437d-5501-9d91-0173648f69f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47510a96-f323-5933-b408-18ebc0d385e2" :answer/id #uuid "47510a96-f323-5933-b408-18ebc0d385e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fd3c60d-64f1-59ef-990a-4ae04dc3e8c7" :answer/id #uuid "7fd3c60d-64f1-59ef-990a-4ae04dc3e8c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f39009f-6a2e-5d88-a632-2c103dc99418" :answer/id #uuid "7f39009f-6a2e-5d88-a632-2c103dc99418" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e680698-5ff8-54db-b218-a63ea07e3ee5" :answer/id #uuid "6e680698-5ff8-54db-b218-a63ea07e3ee5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53d98170-437d-5501-9d91-0173648f69f5" :answer/id #uuid "53d98170-437d-5501-9d91-0173648f69f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073880 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fed5c231-48f8-530b-a66d-407d2c45633b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fed5c231-48f8-530b-a66d-407d2c45633b" :question/id #uuid "fed5c231-48f8-530b-a66d-407d2c45633b" :question/math-academy-id "q-60250" :question/problem "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nA student makes a mixture having $\\frac{4}{9}$ grams of ginger for each gram of glucose to make his own energy drink. Therefore, the energy drink has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ grams of ginger to $\\boxed{}$ grams of glucose." :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{4}{9}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n4:9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the energy drink has a ratio of $4$ grams of ginger to $9$ grams of glucose." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-adf5e13e-d3c5-59f6-8423-d12c85673faf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-adf5e13e-d3c5-59f6-8423-d12c85673faf" :answer-field/id #uuid "adf5e13e-d3c5-59f6-8423-d12c85673faf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-80b5563d-a832-5f85-beb1-f5023beb53ca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6cced7a0-4aa3-52bc-9f11-947258d1a3be" "answer-7ac161ed-1d7c-54b3-a3a8-e7718d81f9d9" "answer-80b5563d-a832-5f85-beb1-f5023beb53ca" "answer-ef6e0e18-3319-51dc-bd29-cc144c970a2a" "answer-42896cb7-0d0b-54cc-969c-bb0fda2c6508"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cced7a0-4aa3-52bc-9f11-947258d1a3be" :answer/id #uuid "6cced7a0-4aa3-52bc-9f11-947258d1a3be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$13$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ac161ed-1d7c-54b3-a3a8-e7718d81f9d9" :answer/id #uuid "7ac161ed-1d7c-54b3-a3a8-e7718d81f9d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ and $13$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80b5563d-a832-5f85-beb1-f5023beb53ca" :answer/id #uuid "80b5563d-a832-5f85-beb1-f5023beb53ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ and $9$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef6e0e18-3319-51dc-bd29-cc144c970a2a" :answer/id #uuid "ef6e0e18-3319-51dc-bd29-cc144c970a2a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ and $9$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42896cb7-0d0b-54cc-969c-bb0fda2c6508" :answer/id #uuid "42896cb7-0d0b-54cc-969c-bb0fda2c6508" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8c4f25cf-0173-54ec-98c6-ab10b632fa9a" :question/id #uuid "8c4f25cf-0173-54ec-98c6-ab10b632fa9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-60256" :question/problem "![](images/06/06931fae92045635d523614dce24063856209b1f04987471b9de183a3ccce4a2.png)\n\nIf the ratio of rhombuses to total shapes is $\\frac{3}{\\boxed{}}$ then what is the missing number?" :question/worked-solution "We count the number of rhombuses. We see that there are $3$ rhombuses.\n\n We count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $7$ shapes.\n\nHence, the ratio of circles to triangles is$\\frac{3}{7}$\n\nSo the missing number is $7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-260e99a3-e5e1-53cf-915e-ef78d3294c9f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-260e99a3-e5e1-53cf-915e-ef78d3294c9f" :answer-field/id #uuid "260e99a3-e5e1-53cf-915e-ef78d3294c9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c434fe79-4413-5270-a27f-9ddb3e2c1623" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36eea84d-8adf-5277-ab85-88e996c1fbca" "answer-3ccb5484-6c71-5479-8103-efc8575ddd3e" "answer-f9df7a6a-2bf6-55ee-9e50-cffb838757e3" "answer-c434fe79-4413-5270-a27f-9ddb3e2c1623" "answer-0f4e2340-8ee0-5351-9fb5-c525dfce930d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36eea84d-8adf-5277-ab85-88e996c1fbca" :answer/id #uuid "36eea84d-8adf-5277-ab85-88e996c1fbca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ccb5484-6c71-5479-8103-efc8575ddd3e" :answer/id #uuid "3ccb5484-6c71-5479-8103-efc8575ddd3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9df7a6a-2bf6-55ee-9e50-cffb838757e3" :answer/id #uuid "f9df7a6a-2bf6-55ee-9e50-cffb838757e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c434fe79-4413-5270-a27f-9ddb3e2c1623" :answer/id #uuid "c434fe79-4413-5270-a27f-9ddb3e2c1623" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f4e2340-8ee0-5351-9fb5-c525dfce930d" :answer/id #uuid "0f4e2340-8ee0-5351-9fb5-c525dfce930d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-32dcf3be-e756-5d49-a23a-c41d074aff19" :activity/id #uuid "32dcf3be-e756-5d49-a23a-c41d074aff19" :activity/title "Writing Ratios Using Fractions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050481 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-37ee238c-3593-502f-845f-f9c2b74cd9d1" "step-73d398fa-e284-584b-af53-0ec2a7adc313" "step-4104b582-02c9-5a3d-a68c-63888ab13e51"] :activity/first-step "step-37ee238c-3593-502f-845f-f9c2b74cd9d1" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-37ee238c-3593-502f-845f-f9c2b74cd9d1" :step/id #uuid "37ee238c-3593-502f-845f-f9c2b74cd9d1" :step/content "question-0b38d5e8-3d9c-538c-a4ad-3e7a464487ac" :step/next "step-73d398fa-e284-584b-af53-0ec2a7adc313" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-73d398fa-e284-584b-af53-0ec2a7adc313" :step/id #uuid "73d398fa-e284-584b-af53-0ec2a7adc313" :step/content "question-fed5c231-48f8-530b-a66d-407d2c45633b" :step/next "step-4104b582-02c9-5a3d-a68c-63888ab13e51" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4104b582-02c9-5a3d-a68c-63888ab13e51" :step/id #uuid "4104b582-02c9-5a3d-a68c-63888ab13e51" :step/content "question-8c4f25cf-0173-54ec-98c6-ab10b632fa9a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157433 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-55bdf128-1307-57a2-a09e-523ed9c58971" "question-a4985131-38a1-553b-8a59-bf4137759de2" "question-7c744e92-6824-57b8-b5de-89c3c18659be" "question-d6227e18-efad-598b-bec8-32e2a28de5a3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157043 :question/problem "Suppose $\\mathbf a=[7,\\, 2,\\, 4]^T$ and $\\mathbf b=[2,\\, 3,\\, 1]^T.$ Find the Euclidean distance $d_2$ between $\\mathbf a$ and $\\mathbf b.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Euclidean distance is defined as\n\n$$\nd_2(\\mathbf a,\\mathbf b) =\\|\\mathbf a-\\mathbf b\\|_2\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $\\mathbf v,$\n\n$$\n\\|\\mathbf v\\|_2 = \\sqrt{\\sum_{i=1}^N |v_i|^2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{2}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{2} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]‖}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{|7-2{|}^{2}+|2-3{|}^{2}+|4-1{|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35} \\\\  & ≈5.916,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157434 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5380f139-fe32-542e-ba7e-191d7abaa184" "question-c95e267e-85b4-5649-968c-53ba871cff30" "question-c6fc9a2a-2dca-5aed-a889-2bc4c863a299" "question-f3e294b9-f845-51ae-87f3-5926acf855f0" "question-83af6a91-b190-50f3-bc76-025dc5091d7d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157040 :question/problem "Suppose $\\mathbf a=[6,\\, -1,\\,2]^T$ and $\\mathbf b=[4,\\, -4,\\,0]^T.$ Find the Manhattan distance $d_1$ between $\\mathbf a$ and $\\mathbf b.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Manhattan distance is defined as\n\n$$\nd_1(\\mathbf a,\\mathbf b) =\\|\\mathbf a-\\mathbf b\\|_1\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $\\mathbf v,$\n\n$$\n\\|\\mathbf v\\|_1 = \\sum_{i=1}^N |v_i|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{1}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{1} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]‖}_{1} \\\\  & =|6-4|+|-1-(-4)|+|2-0| \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157435 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cd8b6d86-5eba-5e13-9d83-5bea3e076943" "question-2ca9d6e1-42a8-5184-8cd9-770775f3f1b2" "question-ae95185c-810c-50b4-b278-d16c314036aa" "question-f4c50ce1-0092-5528-9c12-822dbb56b8d9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157041 :question/problem "Suppose $\\mathbf a=[6,\\, -3,\\, 2]^T,$ and $\\mathbf b=[7,\\, -1,\\, 1]^T,$ and $p=4.$ Find the Minkowski distance $d_p$ between $\\mathbf a$ and $\\mathbf b.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Minkowski distance is defined as\n\n$$\nd_p(\\mathbf a,\\mathbf b) =\\|\\mathbf a-\\mathbf b\\|_p\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $\\mathbf v,$\n\n$$\n\\|\\mathbf v\\|_p = \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^N |v_i|^p \\right)^{1/p}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{4}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{4} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]‖}_{4} \\\\  & ={(|6-7{|}^{4}+|-3-(-1){|}^{4}+|2-1{|}^{4})}^{1/4} \\\\  & ={18}^{1/4} \\\\  & ≈2.060,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157436 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-78d962fb-98a1-54a9-be40-612e78bd3a7f" "question-e36e927d-aa55-5840-81c8-aa7b916f3c2f" "question-79a48270-e1b9-5009-9c26-f6b63d86b07c" "question-7ac6fcb3-d9b4-5799-8b69-524dd3ce6133"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157042 :question/problem "Suppose $\\mathbf a=[-2,\\, 6,\\, -7]^T$ and $\\mathbf b=[8,\\, -9,\\, -9]^T.$ Find the Chebyshev distance $d_\\infty$ between $\\mathbf a$ and $\\mathbf b.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Chebyshev distance is defined as\n\n$$\nd_\\infty(\\mathbf a,\\mathbf b) =\\|\\mathbf a-\\mathbf b\\|_\\infty\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $\\mathbf v,$\n\n$$\n\\|\\mathbf v\\|_\\infty = \\operatorname{max}(|v_1|,|v_2|,\\ldots, |v_N|).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{\\infty }(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & =max(|-2-8|,|6-(-9)|,|-7-(-9)|) \\\\  & =max(10,15,2) \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-55bdf128-1307-57a2-a09e-523ed9c58971" :question/id #uuid "55bdf128-1307-57a2-a09e-523ed9c58971" :question/math-academy-id "q-254851" :question/problem "Suppose $a=[2,\\,6]^{T}$ and $b=[5,\\,3]^{T}.$ Find the Euclidean distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\nRounded to three decimal places, ${d}_{2}(a,b)≈$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Euclidean distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{2}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{2}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{2} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]‖}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{|2-5{|}^{2}+|6-3{|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & ≈4.243.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de7e374a-e6ed-5411-8341-4e4bb667ce86"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de7e374a-e6ed-5411-8341-4e4bb667ce86" :answer-field/id #uuid "de7e374a-e6ed-5411-8341-4e4bb667ce86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f12aa8ac-db2d-511d-a369-95db4ab320ec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f12aa8ac-db2d-511d-a369-95db4ab320ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f12aa8ac-db2d-511d-a369-95db4ab320ec" :answer/id #uuid "f12aa8ac-db2d-511d-a369-95db4ab320ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.243" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a4985131-38a1-553b-8a59-bf4137759de2" :question/id #uuid "a4985131-38a1-553b-8a59-bf4137759de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-254843" :question/problem "Suppose $a=[2,\\,1,\\,4]^{T}$ and $b=[1,\\,3,\\,5]^{T}.$ Find the Euclidean distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\nRounded to three decimal places, ${d}_{2}(a,b)≈$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Euclidean distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{2}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{2}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{2} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]‖}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{|2-1{|}^{2}+|1-3{|}^{2}+|4-5{|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6} \\\\  & ≈2.449.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-90f5fe7e-ef85-51aa-90be-01d6e9471ed5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-90f5fe7e-ef85-51aa-90be-01d6e9471ed5" :answer-field/id #uuid "90f5fe7e-ef85-51aa-90be-01d6e9471ed5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-15bb2856-4f40-543e-9b23-e1e8ec158568" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15bb2856-4f40-543e-9b23-e1e8ec158568"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15bb2856-4f40-543e-9b23-e1e8ec158568" :answer/id #uuid "15bb2856-4f40-543e-9b23-e1e8ec158568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.449" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c744e92-6824-57b8-b5de-89c3c18659be" :question/id #uuid "7c744e92-6824-57b8-b5de-89c3c18659be" :question/math-academy-id "q-254852" :question/problem "Suppose $a=[4,\\,6]^{T}$ and $b=[2,\\,-2]^{T}.$ Find the Euclidean distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\nRounded to three decimal places, ${d}_{2}(a,b)≈$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Euclidean distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{2}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{2}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{2} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]‖}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{|4-2{|}^{2}+|6-(-2){|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{68} \\\\  & ≈8.246.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1a4bfe98-e47c-5ff6-99b2-15d5e97e7b17"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1a4bfe98-e47c-5ff6-99b2-15d5e97e7b17" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a4bfe98-e47c-5ff6-99b2-15d5e97e7b17" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d2d0f71a-5522-5969-b785-b10e460713ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2d0f71a-5522-5969-b785-b10e460713ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2d0f71a-5522-5969-b785-b10e460713ee" :answer/id #uuid "d2d0f71a-5522-5969-b785-b10e460713ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.246" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157708 :question/problem "Suppose $a=[5,\\,1]^{T}$ and $b=[3,\\,-2]^{T}.$ Find the Euclidean distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\nRounded to three decimal places, ${d}_{2}(a,b)≈$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Euclidean distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{2}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{2}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{2} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]‖}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{|5-3{|}^{2}+|1-(-2){|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\  & ≈3.606.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186154798 :answer-field/correct "answer-b44ec29c-504d-5803-b493-2cf59a287bf9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b44ec29c-504d-5803-b493-2cf59a287bf9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b44ec29c-504d-5803-b493-2cf59a287bf9" :answer/id #uuid "b44ec29c-504d-5803-b493-2cf59a287bf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.606" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d6227e18-efad-598b-bec8-32e2a28de5a3" :question/id #uuid "d6227e18-efad-598b-bec8-32e2a28de5a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-254842" :question/problem "Suppose $a=[-1,\\,1,\\,0]^{T}$ and $b=[2,\\,3,\\,1]^{T}.$ Find the Euclidean distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\nRounded to three decimal places, ${d}_{2}(a,b)≈$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Euclidean distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{2}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{2}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{2} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]‖}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{|-1-2{|}^{2}+|1-3{|}^{2}+|0-1{|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\  & ≈3.742.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64d75463-e711-5175-900d-bcfa3b3c7369"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64d75463-e711-5175-900d-bcfa3b3c7369" :answer-field/id #uuid "64d75463-e711-5175-900d-bcfa3b3c7369" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5565d5eb-258d-5c57-abf0-b6d273e3c896" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5565d5eb-258d-5c57-abf0-b6d273e3c896"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5565d5eb-258d-5c57-abf0-b6d273e3c896" :answer/id #uuid "5565d5eb-258d-5c57-abf0-b6d273e3c896" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.742" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5380f139-fe32-542e-ba7e-191d7abaa184" :question/id #uuid "5380f139-fe32-542e-ba7e-191d7abaa184" :question/math-academy-id "q-254862" :question/problem "Suppose $a=[1,\\,4,\\,-2]^{T}$ and $b=[2,\\,5,\\,3]^{T}.$ Find the Manhattan distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\n${d}_{1}(a,b)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Manhattan distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{1}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{1}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{1}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{1} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]‖}_{1} \\\\  & =|1-2|+|4-5|+|-2-3| \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-808c45fe-82b7-5271-9482-5eb4b030372f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-808c45fe-82b7-5271-9482-5eb4b030372f" :answer-field/id #uuid "808c45fe-82b7-5271-9482-5eb4b030372f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-86f9cffe-0437-53b4-9b46-e03c290d7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86f9cffe-0437-53b4-9b46-e03c290d7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/